const QUESTIONS = [{"q":"You clean a bedroom with a ceiling fan, shelves and a carpet. Which order is best?","opts":["Vacuum the carpet first, then dust the shelves and the fan.","Dust the fan and shelves first, then vacuum the carpet last.","Wipe the shelves, vacuum the carpet, then dust the fan.","Dust the fan, vacuum the carpet, then wipe the shelves last."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":0},{"q":"Your 2-hour job has a very dirty bathroom. After 70 minutes you are still in it. The family is at home. What do you do?","opts":["Keep scrubbing until the bathroom is perfect, then clean other rooms with the time left.","Stop now and rush through every room so nothing is left untouched.","Ask your supervisor to add an hour, and keep scrubbing the bathroom until it is finished.","Tell the customer time is short, agree which areas come first, and do those well."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":1},{"q":"The customer gives you an old bottle with no label and asks you to use it on the bathroom tiles. What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse it, use your company products, and explain you cannot use unknown chemicals.","Test it on a small hidden spot, then use it if the tile looks fine.","Use it with gloves and an open window, because the customer owns it.","Use it only on the floor, away from your own products."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":2},{"q":"You finished the toilet. Now you will wipe the kitchen counter. Which cloth do you use?","opts":["The toilet cloth, after rinsing it well in hot water.","Any cloth, because you only used it on the outside of the toilet.","The kitchen-colour cloth, kept separate from the toilet cloth all job.","The bathroom sink cloth, because it is cleaner than the toilet cloth."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":3},{"q":"A customer shouts that the bedroom is not clean. You believe you cleaned it well. What do you do?","opts":["Answer back firmly that you did your best, so she understands your side.","Stay calm, listen, fix what she points out, and tell the supervisor if abuse continues.","Say nothing and walk out of the room until she calms down and stops shouting, to finish sooner.","Clean the whole room again and skip other rooms, to prove to her it was clean."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":4},{"q":"How do you clean a stainless steel fridge door without streaks?","opts":["Wipe with damp microfiber along the grain, then buff dry.","Spray glass cleaner and wipe in circles until it shines.","Scrub the marks with a rough sponge, then rinse with water.","Wipe with a wet cloth in circles and let it air-dry."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":5},{"q":"You break a glass in the kitchen while the customer is out. You could hide the pieces and nobody would know. What do you do?","opts":["Throw the pieces away and say nothing, because glass is cheap.","Buy a similar glass yourself and put it back without telling anyone, so you finish sooner.","Clean it up safely and only mention it if the customer asks.","Clean up safely, then report it honestly to the customer and the company."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":6},{"q":"The customer asks you to clean her whole garage, which is not in the booking. You have little time left. What do you do?","opts":["Do it fast and leave the half-cleaned rooms as they are, since she asked you.","Say yes and work extra time without telling anyone, because you want her to stay happy.","Explain politely it is not booked, finish your tasks, and suggest she books it through the company.","Say no firmly and keep cleaning, without giving a reason, to avoid a long talk."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":7},{"q":"A natural marble bathroom floor has dull marks. Which product is safe to use?","opts":["A pH-neutral stone cleaner or mild soap, then dry the floor.","Vinegar mixed in water, because it lifts marks from natural stone floors.","Diluted acid toilet cleaner, to remove the dull marks, then rinse it.","Bleach in hot water, then mop it dry with a clean cloth."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":8},{"q":"In training, the trainer shouts that your bathroom work is poor. You feel it is unfair. What do you do?","opts":["Explain loudly why the trainer is wrong, so everyone hears your side.","Stay calm, fix what the trainer showed, and ask how to do better.","Stay quiet, finish the day, and tell other trainees the trainer is unfair.","Say sorry, then keep doing it your own way when the trainer leaves."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":9},{"q":"The customer says to use her own quiet vacuum instead of the company machine. What do you do?","opts":["Use hers, because the customer decides how her own home is cleaned.","Use hers while she is watching, and the company machine when she leaves.","Use the company machine only in the last room so she hears less noise.","Politely explain the company machine is required, and tell your supervisor if she insists."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":10},{"q":"How do you mop a large tiled floor correctly?","opts":["Soak the floor with water, mop once, and leave it to dry, to save time.","Mop from the door toward the room, then walk back over the wet floor.","Sweep or vacuum first, then mop from the far corner back to the exit.","Mop first to lift the dust, then sweep the dry dirt after."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":11},{"q":"The van is 40 minutes late to collect you for a job, and the customer starts calling you. What do you do?","opts":["Call the supervisor at once, so the customer is updated, and follow the new plan.","Take a taxi yourself to arrive faster, and ask the company to pay you back later.","Wait quietly, because the van timing is not your job to manage.","Tell the customer the van company is the problem, so she accepts the delay."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":12},{"q":"A new customer asks what your last customer's house looked like and how much she paid. What do you do?","opts":["Share general details without any names, to be friendly and polite.","Show photos from your phone, so she sees the quality you give.","Describe the house but do not mention how much she paid.","Politely say you do not share other customers' details."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":13},{"q":"How do you clean a bathroom mirror without streaks?","opts":["Spray a lot of cleaner on the mirror and wipe with paper towel.","Spray a little cleaner on a microfiber cloth, wipe, then buff dry.","Wipe with a wet kitchen sponge and let it dry in the air, because it is easier.","Use the damp sink cloth, because it is soft."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":14},{"q":"You feel very sick and weak before a 4-hour job and cannot work safely. What do you do?","opts":["Go to the job anyway and rest when the customer is not looking.","Say nothing and do only the easy rooms during the job, because it is quicker.","Tell the supervisor before the job, so another cleaner can be arranged.","Ask a friend to go in your place, so the booking is not lost."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":15},{"q":"The wife wants the bedroom cleaned first, and her husband wants the kitchen first. Both are at home. What do you do?","opts":["Politely ask them to agree on one order, and start with it.","Start with whoever spoke to you first and ignore what the other says.","Clean a little of each room, so both feel satisfied.","Follow the person who looks more upset, to avoid an argument."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":16},{"q":"You need to remove limescale and also kill germs in a small shower room. What is the safe method?","opts":["Spray the acid descaler and bleach together so they work at the same time.","Put bleach on top of the descaler foam, because the foam holds it on the wall.","Mix both in a bucket with cold water, so the smell is weaker.","Use one product, rinse the area well, open the window, then use the next product."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":17},{"q":"Cleaners in the accommodation say they will all refuse tomorrow's jobs for better pay and ask you to join. What do you do?","opts":["Join them, because a group has more power than one person alone.","Do not join, go to your job, and raise pay concerns through the supervisor.","Say you are sick on that day, so you do not have to choose a side.","Join quietly, but still clean if the customer asks you to."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":18},{"q":"A colleague takes cash from a customer to clean one extra room privately, and asks you to stay quiet. What do you do?","opts":["Stay quiet, because it is small money and the customer is happy.","Tell the colleague to stop, and say nothing more if they agree.","Report it to the supervisor, even though your colleague asked you not to.","Tell the other cleaners but not the supervisor, so the colleague feels ashamed."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":19},{"q":"Burnt grease is inside the customer's oven. When and how do you use the oven cleaner?","opts":["While the oven is very hot, so the burnt grease melts away faster.","With the oven switched on low, so the cleaner works better on grease.","Only when it is off and cool, wearing gloves with a window open.","Also on the oven light and electric parts, so nothing is missed."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":20},{"q":"Your supervisor says your quality is poor, so you must do retraining with a salary deduction. You feel it is unfair. What do you do?","opts":["Accept the retraining, ask what to improve, and raise any fairness concern through HR.","Do the retraining but only the minimum, since the deduction is already decided.","Do the retraining but tell other cleaners it is unfair, to get their support.","Ask to skip it, and promise to improve on your own next week."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":21},{"q":"A customer asks you to stand on a wobbly chair to clean a high window and says it is fine. What do you do?","opts":["Stand on it carefully and hold the wall, because she accepts the risk herself.","Ask her to hold the chair while you clean the window quickly.","Skip the window and say nothing about it, to avoid an argument.","Politely refuse it, and use a safe step stool or ladder instead."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":22},{"q":"How do you clean the inside of a fridge?","opts":["Spray strong cleaner over the shelves and food, then wipe it all clean.","Take out food, wipe shelves with mild soapy water, dry, then refill.","Pour hot water inside the fridge to melt the dirt away.","Leave the food inside and wipe around it, to save time and effort."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":23},{"q":"The van driver shouts at you and other cleaners for being slow. You feel insulted. What do you do?","opts":["Stay calm, then report his behaviour to the supervisor with details.","Shout back at him, so he knows you will not accept that.","Refuse to sit in his van tomorrow, and use a taxi instead.","Write about him in the cleaners' group chat to get support."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":24},{"q":"Red juice spills on a customer's light carpet. What is the first step?","opts":["Rub hard with a wet cloth so the colour leaves quickly.","Pour hot water on it to wash the colour away at once.","Blot with a clean dry cloth, working from the edge inward.","Scrub with a hard brush so the stain does not set in."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":25},{"q":"You find cash under a sofa cushion while vacuuming. The customer is out and nobody saw you. What do you do?","opts":["Put it back under the cushion and say nothing, so nobody blames you.","Tell the customer and supervisor about it, and hand it over as they direct.","Keep it safe in your bag until the customer asks if she lost anything.","Count it, take a small reward, and give the rest back, because it is quicker."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":26},{"q":"Your job is finished but the pickup van is 30 minutes late and the driver does not answer. What do you do?","opts":["Walk to the main road and find a taxi with your own money.","Wait quietly, because the driver will come when he can.","Ask the customer to drive you back to the accommodation, to finish sooner.","Call the supervisor, say where you are, and wait safely for instructions."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":27},{"q":"After a sandstorm, thick dust covers the windowsills and furniture. What do you do first?","opts":["Wipe it hard with a dry cloth, so all the dust leaves at once.","Spray water on the dust and wipe, because water holds the sand.","Vacuum or soft-brush the loose sand first, then wipe with damp microfiber.","Flick the dust off with a duster, then clean what stays."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":28},{"q":"Your accommodation supervisor wakes everyone very early and shouts, and you feel tired for jobs. What do you do?","opts":["Follow the schedule and raise the issue with HR, giving clear details.","Tell the other residents to ignore the early wake-up call, so you finish sooner.","Arrive late to jobs to show your supervisor that it is a problem.","Complain to customers about the accommodation during the job."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":29},{"q":"A customer likes your work and offers extra cash if you come privately on your day off, without the company. What do you do?","opts":["Accept, because it is your free time.","Politely decline, and keep working only through the company.","Accept just once, to see how it goes, because it is less work.","Decline, but tell your colleagues so they can take the job."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":30},{"q":"You will use strong bathroom cleaner in a small room with no window. What do you do?","opts":["Wear gloves only and work faster to finish the job quickly.","Close the door, so the smell stays inside the room.","Wear a mask only and keep spraying until the whole room is done.","Wear gloves, keep the door open, use little cleaner, and take breaks."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":31},{"q":"The job needs the floor scrubbing machine, but it is heavy and you do not like using it. What do you do?","opts":["Use it as trained, and ask for help if you cannot use it safely.","Mop by hand instead, since the floor looks the same to the customer.","Use it only if the supervisor is checking your work that day.","Tell the customer the machine is not needed for her floor."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":32},{"q":"On a 4-hour job, your partner leaves 40 minutes early and asks you to say they stayed full time. What do you do?","opts":["Agree, because you will finish the work alone anyway.","Say nothing unless someone asks you.","Do not cover for them, and tell the supervisor what happened.","Agree this time and ask them not to do it again, to save time."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":33},{"q":"You must clean behind a TV and its cables. What is the safe first step?","opts":["Wipe the cables with a damp cloth, since they are covered in plastic.","Spray cleaner on a cloth, then wipe the plugs.","Turn the TV off with the remote and start cleaning.","Switch off and unplug it from the wall first, then dust dry."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":34},{"q":"Another cleaner says rush to finish early because early finishers get praise. You know quality earns incentives. What do you do?","opts":["Rush, because finishing early is what gets rewarded and praised.","Follow the cleaning steps and time plan, because quality earns incentives.","Rush the first rooms and slow down when you reach the end, because it is easier.","Rush when the customer is out, and slow down when watched."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":35},{"q":"You ran out of time and did not clean the oven. The checklist says done and nobody will check. What do you do?","opts":["Tick it and promise yourself you will clean it properly next visit.","Leave it unticked, but say nothing to the customer about it.","Tick it, because you did other tasks very well and saved time.","Report honestly that the oven was not done, and say why."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":36},{"q":"How do you vacuum a carpet correctly?","opts":["Vacuum slowly in overlapping rows, from the far side toward the door.","Move the vacuum fast in circles to cover more space quickly.","Vacuum once only in the middle of the room, where people walk.","Vacuum wet spots as well, to help them dry faster."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":37},{"q":"A new cleaner keeps saying the company is bad and urges others to do less work. What do you do?","opts":["Agree to keep the peace, and do slightly less work yourself.","Argue with them in front of everyone, so others hear you.","Keep working properly, avoid the talk, and report concerns to the supervisor.","Avoid them completely and tell nobody, so you stay out of trouble."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":38},{"q":"At the end of a 4-hour booking, the customer says you can leave 40 minutes early because the house looks fine. What do you do?","opts":["Leave now, because the customer decides when the work is finished.","Go through the checklist, finish open areas, and confirm with the company before leaving.","Leave now and do not mention it to anyone later.","Stay but rest until the booked time ends, then leave."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":39},{"q":"Which order is best for cleaning a kitchen?","opts":["Start with the stove, then the floor, then the counters last.","Cabinet tops and counters first, then stove and sink, then the floor last.","Clean the sink first, then the cabinet tops, then the stove and floor.","Mop the floor first, then wipe the counters and sink above it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":40},{"q":"The customer says her old cleaner finished in half the time and tells you to hurry. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the corners and edges to match what her old cleaner did.","Work fast while she watches, then slow down when she leaves.","Stay polite, keep your cleaning steps and quality, and tell her what you will finish in the booked time.","Tell her the old cleaner must have done poor work."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":41},{"q":"A customer asks you to take off your mask and gloves because they look unfriendly. You are using strong cleaner. What do you do?","opts":["Take them off to be polite, and put them back when she leaves.","Politely keep them on, explain it is a safety rule, and continue.","Remove the mask only, and keep the gloves on, because it is easier.","Take both off but use less cleaner."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":42},{"q":"How do you clean a dirty microwave inside?","opts":["Spray strong oven cleaner inside, close the door, and wipe after ten minutes.","Scrub it with a steel wool pad to remove all dried food.","Heat a bowl of water to make steam, wait a minute, then wipe the walls.","Wipe it with a cloth soaked in bleach, then close the door."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":43},{"q":"After the job, the customer calls to say you missed the bedroom corners, and your supervisor asks you about it. What do you do?","opts":["Say you cleaned them, and the customer is wrong.","Say the van driver rushed you, so it is his fault.","Answer honestly, say what happened, and accept a quick return visit to fix it if asked.","Say nothing and ignore the message until next week."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":44},{"q":"How do you clean a dusty window track?","opts":["Spray cleaner in the track and leave it to dry on its own, to save time.","Wipe the track with a damp cloth first, then brush the dirt out.","Pour water into the track and wipe it with a dry cloth.","Vacuum or brush the loose dirt out first, then wipe with a damp cloth."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":45},{"q":"A friendly customer asks for your personal phone number so she can book you directly next time. What do you do?","opts":["Politely say bookings must go through the company, and do not give your number.","Give it to her, because it is only for one friendly customer.","Give your number, but ask her to also book through the company.","Say you will message her later, once the job is finished and you are free."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":46},{"q":"You arrive for a job, nobody is home, and the door is locked. The customer does not answer your calls. What do you do?","opts":["Call the supervisor, report what happened, and wait safely for instructions.","Go back to the van and say nothing about it.","Try to open a window and enter, to save the booking.","Wait one hour, then ask a neighbour to open the door."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":47},{"q":"A fabric sofa has dust and one small drink stain. What is the right method?","opts":["Spray bleach on the stain to remove it fast.","Vacuum it first, then blot the stain gently with a little mild cleaner, following the label.","Brush the stain hard with a stiff brush.","Wet the whole sofa with soapy water and rub hard."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":48},{"q":"Two trainers show different ways to clean a bathroom sink, and both are angry about mistakes. What do you do?","opts":["Mix both ways, so both trainers are partly happy.","Politely ask your main trainer which method to follow, and use only that one.","Follow the louder trainer, to stop the shouting.","Pick the faster way and hope nobody notices."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":49},{"q":"You want to post before-and-after photos of a customer's home to your friends. No face or name shows. What do you do?","opts":["Do not post them. Customers' homes are private, even without faces.","Send them only to close friends, not in public, because it is easier.","Post them after you remove the address from the caption.","Post them, because no face or name is shown."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":50},{"q":"You spray disinfectant on a toilet seat. When do you wipe it?","opts":["After 20 seconds, which is enough for every product.","Only after it dries completely on the surface, so you finish sooner.","After the contact time on the label, so the germs are killed.","Immediately, because wiping fast gives the best shine."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":51},{"q":"You cut your hand on broken glass while cleaning. It bleeds a lot, and 90 minutes of the job remain. What do you do?","opts":["Cover it with a glove and keep working until the job is finished.","Wrap it tightly in tape and finish the job, then report it after.","Wash it quickly and continue, so you do not delay the customer.","Stop, press a clean cloth on the cut, and tell the supervisor right away."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":52},{"q":"A customer asks you to move a very heavy wardrobe alone so you can clean behind it. What do you do?","opts":["Politely say you cannot move heavy furniture alone, and clean around it safely.","Empty it first, then move it and put it back.","Push it a little with your leg and clean only the middle, because it is less work.","Slide it carefully yourself, because she asked politely."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":53},{"q":"How do you use a squeegee on a shower glass wall?","opts":["Pull from top to bottom in straight lines, wiping the blade after each pass.","Start at the bottom and push the water upward.","Move it side to side in curves and leave the water at the bottom, to save time.","Press hard and go over the same place many times without wiping the blade."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":54},{"q":"You feel dizzy from a strong chemical smell in a closed bathroom. What do you do?","opts":["Close the door to keep the smell inside the room, then rest a minute.","Cover your nose with a cloth, and continue with the job.","Stop, go to fresh air, drink water, and tell the supervisor before you continue.","Keep working fast to finish the bathroom sooner, then take fresh air."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":55},{"q":"The customer tells you to use the red toilet cloth on her kitchen counter because it looks clean. What do you do?","opts":["Use it, because she knows her home best.","Use it once on a clean spot, and then wash it.","Use it only when she is watching, and the kitchen cloth when she leaves.","Politely explain the company rule, use the kitchen cloth, and tell your supervisor if she insists."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":56},{"q":"You must clean a high shelf. What is the safe way to do it?","opts":["Stand on the top step to reach further, because it is quicker.","Stand on a chair with wheels, to move along quickly.","Put the stool on a rug, so it does not slip.","Use a stable step stool on a flat floor and never overreach."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":57},{"q":"Your partner works very slowly, and you will not finish on time. What do you do?","opts":["Work slower too, so the result is fair.","Politely ask them to speed up, share the tasks, and tell the supervisor if time is still at risk.","Do their work silently and say nothing.","Complain to the customer about your partner."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":58},{"q":"You see a colleague put a small perfume bottle from the customer's dresser into their bag. What do you do?","opts":["Ask them quietly to put it back, and stay quiet if they do.","Tell the other cleaners but not the supervisor, because it is less work.","Say nothing, because it may be a gift.","Report it to the supervisor right away, and do not take part."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":59},{"q":"What is the right order to clean a living room?","opts":["Vacuum the floor first, then dust the shelves above it.","Dust the TV area, vacuum, then wipe the shelves last.","Wipe the coffee table first, then dust the high shelves.","Dust high shelves and the TV area first, then sofas, then vacuum the floor last."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":60},{"q":"The customer asks you to also clean a small extra bedroom that is not booked. You have 20 minutes left. What do you do?","opts":["Say it is not booked, finish your tasks, and suggest booking through the company.","Say no firmly and give no explanation, because the time is nearly over.","Do it quickly and leave your last booked room half finished and untidy.","Say yes and stay late without telling anyone, to keep her happy."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":61},{"q":"You find a bottle of strong cleaner under the sink with a handwritten note instead of a label. What do you do?","opts":["Use it on the sink, because the note says what it is.","Pour a little in your own bottle to use later.","Smell it first and use it if it seems fine.","Do not use it, and tell the supervisor that an unlabeled chemical is in the home."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":62},{"q":"Which method is safe for a sealed granite kitchen counter?","opts":["Use a rough pad and strong acid to remove marks.","Leave it wet to dry on its own after wiping, because it is quicker.","Scrub with bleach every day to keep it white.","Wipe with warm water and a few drops of mild dish soap, then dry."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":63},{"q":"The customer shouts that the price is too high and blames you in front of her family. What do you do?","opts":["Offer her a discount from your own pay, to calm her down quickly.","Stay calm, say prices are handled by the company, and tell the supervisor.","Argue that the price is fair and tell her that she must pay it now.","Stop cleaning and wait outside until she calms down and apologises to you."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":64},{"q":"A chrome bathroom tap has white limescale. What is the safest way to clean it?","opts":["Use a descaler made for taps by the label, then rinse and dry with a soft cloth.","Use strong toilet acid and leave it on for ten minutes.","Wipe it with a wet cloth and let it dry.","Scrub it with a hard pad until the white marks disappear, because it is less work."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":65},{"q":"The customer asks you to skip the safety sign when mopping because it looks ugly in her hall. What do you do?","opts":["Put it in a corner where it is hidden.","Politely explain the sign is required for safety, and put it up.","Mop quickly so it dries before anyone walks there.","Skip it, and warn the family in person instead, to finish sooner."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":66},{"q":"The van driver drives very fast and you feel unsafe. The other cleaners say nothing. What do you do?","opts":["Get off at the next stop and walk to the job by yourself.","Post a video of the driving in the group chat, to warn the others.","Ask him politely to slow down, and report it to the supervisor.","Say nothing, because the driver knows the roads better than you."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":67},{"q":"Black marks are in the grout of a shower tray. What is the best first step?","opts":["Wipe it with a dry cloth, because grout cannot be cleaned.","Pour bleach and an acid toilet cleaner together on the grout, so you finish sooner.","Apply a suitable grout cleaner by the label, scrub with a soft brush, then rinse.","Use a metal brush to scrape the marks away."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":68},{"q":"You feel tired and do not want to go to a far job tomorrow, but you are not sick. What do you do?","opts":["Go to the job as planned, and talk to the supervisor about the workload.","Say you are sick, so you can stay in your room and rest tomorrow.","Refuse the job and tell everybody that it is too far away for you.","Go, but work slowly to show everybody that you are very tired."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":69},{"q":"A customer gives you a gift bag and asks you to clean her car for it. The car is not booked. What do you do?","opts":["Accept and clean the car quickly after the job.","Thank her politely, decline the extra job, and tell the supervisor about the gift.","Accept the gift but say you will do the car next visit.","Refuse the gift rudely so she will not ask again."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":70},{"q":"What is the safe way to clean a dusty ceiling fan?","opts":["Spray cleaner over the fan and let it drip on the floor.","Wipe the blades while it is still spinning slowly, to save time.","Switch it off, wait until it stops, then wipe each blade from a stable stool.","Shake the dust off the blades over the bed, then vacuum it."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":71},{"q":"Other cleaners will leave 30 minutes early and say the job was finished. They ask you to join. What do you do?","opts":["Stay, but promise your colleagues not to tell anyone what happened later.","Leave 10 minutes early as a compromise, so nobody is upset with you.","Do not join, finish your booked time, and tell the supervisor if they leave.","Join them, because going along with the group is safer than going alone."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":72},{"q":"A customer offers you food and says it is rude to refuse. You are on a tight 2-hour job. What do you do?","opts":["Accept and sit with her family for a long break.","Say you cannot eat anything in customers' homes, in a strict tone, because it is easier.","Take the food and eat it quietly while cleaning.","Thank her warmly, politely decline or keep it very short, and carry on with your tasks."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":73},{"q":"What is the correct way to clean a toilet bowl?","opts":["Apply cleaner under the rim, brush the bowl, flush, then wipe with a separate cloth.","Brush the bowl, then wipe the seat with the kitchen cloth.","Use the same cloth for the bowl and the sink, to save time.","Pour cleaner into the water and flush it without brushing."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":74},{"q":"The van driver drops you at the wrong building, and 25 minutes of your job time are lost. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the bathrooms to make up the time.","Cancel the job and go back to the accommodation.","Call the supervisor at once, tell them the delay, and agree a plan for the shorter time.","Rush through the job to finish on time without telling anyone."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":75},{"q":"Your supervisor says finish the kitchen first, but the customer says finish the bedroom first because guests arrive. What do you do?","opts":["Call the supervisor, explain the customer's need, and follow the agreed order.","Split your time equally between both rooms.","Follow the customer, because she is paying.","Follow the supervisor and ignore the customer's reason, because it is less work."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":76},{"q":"How do you clean a glass dining table without streaks?","opts":["Spray a lot of cleaner and wipe with the kitchen sponge.","Spray a little glass cleaner on a microfiber cloth, wipe, then buff dry.","Wipe with a greasy cloth, then rinse it.","Pour water on it, wipe with a paper napkin, and let it dry, to save time."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":77},{"q":"Traffic made you 35 minutes late to a 4-hour job. The customer is annoyed. What do you do?","opts":["Blame the driver loudly, so the customer is angry at him instead.","Ignore her complaint and start working in the kitchen straight away.","Work extra fast and skip the finishing checks, to catch up.","Apologise once, explain briefly, and plan the work to finish key areas on time."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":78},{"q":"A colleague tells you the address and daily routine of a rich customer to a friend. What do you do?","opts":["Join the conversation so you are not left out.","Tell the colleague to stop, and report it to the supervisor.","Tell the customer directly without telling your supervisor, to finish sooner.","Ignore it, because they are only talking."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":79},{"q":"Which order is best when cleaning a bathroom?","opts":["Mop the floor first, then clean the shower that is above it.","Spray cleaner first, then clean the mirror, sink, shower, toilet, and the floor last.","Clean the sink, then the toilet, then the mirror, then the shower last.","Clean the toilet first, then the mirror and sink, and the shower last."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":80},{"q":"In a 4-hour job, one bedroom is almost clean and the kitchen is extremely dirty. How do you use your time?","opts":["Clean the almost-clean bedroom first, then rush the kitchen at the end.","Leave the clean bedroom out of the job, and tell nobody about it.","Give more time to the dirty kitchen, keep light time for the clean room, and check quality in both.","Give every room the same time, to be fair to each area."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":81},{"q":"The customer says to use her strong cleaner on her wooden cabinets. The label is in a language you cannot read. What do you do?","opts":["Use it, because she knows her own wooden cabinets better than you do.","Use it only on the top of the cabinet, where it cannot be seen.","Use it with a lot of water, so that it is weaker and gentler.","Politely decline, and use your approved product after testing a hidden spot."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":82},{"q":"How do you clean a wooden floor?","opts":["Sweep or vacuum, then mop with a well-wrung damp mop, and dry any wet areas.","Pour water on the floor and mop it until clean.","Scrub with a hard brush and strong cleaner.","Use a steam machine on all areas for 5 minutes each."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":83},{"q":"A customer follows you in each room and criticises every wipe. You feel stressed. What do you do?","opts":["Do everything the way she says, even if it breaks the cleaning steps you learned.","Stay calm, listen, ask what she wants changed, and keep working to your steps.","Work much faster, so that her inspection ends sooner and she leaves.","Tell her to stop watching you, or you will leave the job."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":84},{"q":"What is the best way to avoid damage to a mirror frame when cleaning?","opts":["Spray the cleaner on the cloth, not on the mirror, then wipe from the center.","Use a wet paper towel and press hard on the edges of the frame.","Use bleach to remove all the spots from the frame and the glass.","Spray the cleaner directly and let it run down, so it cleans itself."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":85},{"q":"After the job the customer insists on giving you cash as a tip. What do you do?","opts":["Thank her, politely refuse, and tell the supervisor she wanted to tip.","Take it and share it with your partner, to be fair to them both.","Take it, because she gave it to you freely and happily as a thank you.","Take it, but say nothing about it to anyone at the company."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":86},{"q":"You feel fine but do not want tomorrow's early job. A friend says to pretend to be sick. What do you do?","opts":["Say your phone is broken, so that you miss the early pickup.","Do not pretend. Go to the job, and tell the supervisor if the schedule is a problem.","Pretend to be sick, because one missed day will not matter much.","Arrive late on purpose, so that they replace you for the early job."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":87},{"q":"The stove top is still warm and has dried food. What is the safe way to clean it?","opts":["Scrape it with a metal knife on the burner.","Spray cold water on it while hot to loosen dirt.","Let it cool, remove grates, apply degreaser, wait, then wipe with a cloth.","Pour bleach on it and wait a few minutes."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":88},{"q":"The trainer says your folded cloths are untidy in front of the whole group. What do you do?","opts":["Laugh to hide your embarrassment and do nothing, because it is less work.","Say thank you, fix it, and ask what a good result looks like.","Tell the group the trainer is too strict.","Say the trainer is shouting for no reason."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":89},{"q":"While dusting a desk you see a customer's open bank letter with a large amount. What do you do?","opts":["Mention it to a friend, without any names, because it is easier.","Photograph it in case you need it later.","Dust around it without reading, and keep what you saw private.","Read it quickly, because it was in plain sight."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":90},{"q":"How do you clean the front grille of a split AC?","opts":["Spray bleach on the grille and leave it on for an hour.","Leave it running and wipe the vents while cold air blows out.","Switch it off, vacuum loose dust with a brush, then wipe the grille with a damp cloth.","Spray water inside the AC unit, to wash the dust away."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":91},{"q":"The company vacuum stops working in the middle of a job. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the carpets, and say nothing about the broken vacuum to anyone.","Hide the broken vacuum in the van and mop the whole home instead.","Use the customer's own vacuum without asking her first, to finish on time.","Report it to the supervisor, and clean by hand what you can while you wait."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":92},{"q":"A customer asks you not to wear a cap and shoe covers because it makes her home look messy. What do you do?","opts":["Politely explain the company uniform and hygiene rules, and keep them on.","Remove them for now, then wear them again when she leaves.","Remove the cap but keep the shoe covers on in her home, so you finish sooner.","Remove them only in the living room where she sits and watches."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":93},{"q":"How do you clean a stainless steel kitchen sink?","opts":["Scrub with steel wool until the sink shines like new.","Apply mild cleaner, scrub gently with a soft sponge along the grain, rinse, then dry.","Wipe it with a dry cloth only, without any cleaner or rinse.","Leave bleach in the sink overnight to remove all stains."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":94},{"q":"Your job ended early, and the van will arrive 90 minutes later. The customer says she needs her house quiet. What do you do?","opts":["Walk home alone, because the distance is not very far.","Start another cleaning job privately in the flat next door, for cash.","Stay inside and watch TV quietly, to pass the time until the van arrives.","Tell the supervisor, ask for instructions, and wait politely outside if allowed."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":95},{"q":"A customer asks you to tell the supervisor the house was dirtier than it was, so she can claim a discount. What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse, and report to the supervisor exactly what you saw.","Agree, but ask for a tip first.","Agree, because it is only a small lie.","Say nothing and let the customer talk to the supervisor, to save time."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":96},{"q":"What do you do with the mop and bucket after the job?","opts":["Store the wet mop in a closed bag.","Rinse the mop in the toilet.","Leave dirty water in the bucket until the next job.","Rinse the mop head, empty the dirty water, and let the mop dry before storing."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":97},{"q":"Your room is noisy at night and you cannot sleep before a 4-hour job. What do you do?","opts":["Complain about the accommodation to the customer, during the job.","Arrive late to the job, to show how tired you are.","Shout at the noisy roommates at midnight, so they stop.","Speak politely to the roommates, and tell the accommodation supervisor if it continues."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":98},{"q":"A colleague skips the company floor machine because it is heavy and asks you to do the same. What do you do?","opts":["Use it only when the customer is watching, and skip it otherwise.","Skip it too, because the floor looks fine to you and your colleague.","Use the machine as trained, and report it if your colleague keeps skipping it.","Mop by hand and tell the supervisor that the machine was used."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":99},{"q":"You will clean a bedroom and mop the floor. Why do you dust the furniture first?","opts":["Dust sticks better to a wet floor, so it is easier to remove it later.","The order does not change the result if you clean well enough.","Dust falls down, so the floor is cleaned last and stays clean.","Wet floors make dust easier to see, so you can dust better."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":100},{"q":"The customer points at a streaky mirror and says the job is bad. You are near the end of your time. What do you do?","opts":["Wipe it quickly with the same wet cloth and say it is finished.","Say sorry, fix the mirror properly now, and check other glass surfaces too.","Promise to fix it on your next visit.","Tell her mirrors always look streaky in this light, because it is less work."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":101},{"q":"The customer says her mix of bleach and vinegar works great and asks you to use it in the shower. What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse, explain it is unsafe to mix them, and use your company products.","Mix a smaller amount of each, so that the gas is weaker.","Use it but wear a mask and gloves, to stay safe in the shower.","Use it with the window open, because she has used it many times before."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":102},{"q":"How do you clean a leather sofa?","opts":["Soak it with water and let it dry in the sun, because it is easier.","Spray a bleach cleaner on it and rub hard.","Scrub it with a rough brush to lift the dirt.","Wipe with a soft, slightly damp cloth and mild soap, then dry it."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":103},{"q":"After a hard training week you are told to repeat one day, and you think it is unfair. What do you do?","opts":["Tell other trainees to skip the day with you.","Attend the extra day, learn from it, and raise your concern calmly with HR.","Attend but work slowly, to show you are unhappy.","Refuse to attend until the decision is changed."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":104},{"q":"How do you clean a greasy metal filter from a kitchen hood?","opts":["Soak it in hot water with degreaser, scrub gently, rinse, and dry it before putting it back.","Rinse it and put it back wet so it dries in place.","Spray bleach on it while it is installed.","Wipe it with a dry cloth while it stays fixed in place."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":105},{"q":"You scratch a coffee table while cleaning, and the customer is out. You could cover the mark. What do you do?","opts":["Move the table to a darker corner, so the scratch is less visible.","Tell the supervisor and customer honestly, and follow the company process.","Cover the scratch with a mat, and say nothing to anyone.","Polish it to make the mark less visible, and keep quiet about it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":106},{"q":"The other cleaners leave for the van while you finish your room, and the van starts to leave. What do you do?","opts":["Leave the room half done and run after the van.","Take a random taxi without telling anyone.","Stay and wait quietly, hoping the van returns.","Call the supervisor, explain the situation, and ask for a safe ride plan."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":107},{"q":"How do you clean light switches and door handles?","opts":["Wash them with a very wet cloth.","Skip them, because they are small and clean quickly.","Spray disinfectant on a cloth, wipe, and leave it wet for the label time.","Spray disinfectant directly on the switch for a deeper clean, because it is less work."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":108},{"q":"The supervisor moves you to a later job and you have a personal plan. What do you do?","opts":["Ask a friend to take your place.","Politely explain your concern, and follow the schedule unless the supervisor approves a change.","Ignore the change and go at your old time.","Tell the supervisor you are sick that day."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":109},{"q":"A teenager in the home hides a mess under her bed and asks you not to tell her parents. What do you do?","opts":["Politely say you cannot hide things, and kindly suggest she tells her parents.","Leave it and avoid that room.","Tell her parents at once in front of her.","Clean it quietly and promise not to tell."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":110},{"q":"When should you change the water in your mop bucket?","opts":["Never, if you add more cleaner each time you mop.","Only after every three rooms, whatever the colour of the water.","When it looks dirty, so you do not spread dirt on the floor.","Only at the end of the job, to save time and water."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":111},{"q":"The van brings you back very late, and you have an early job tomorrow. What do you do?","opts":["Skip tomorrow's early job to catch up on your sleep, so you finish sooner.","Arrive late tomorrow and explain that the van caused the delay.","Rest, report the late returns to the supervisor, and be ready on time.","Tell the supervisor you are sick, so they replace you tomorrow."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":112},{"q":"A customer tells you about her family problems. Another customer later asks what she said. What do you do?","opts":["Say you do not discuss customers' private matters.","Say she shared nothing with you, but smile as you say it.","Share a little, since both of the customers are friendly with you.","Tell her only if she promises to keep it a secret from everyone."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":113},{"q":"How do you clean a kitchen bin?","opts":["Clean only the lid and the outside.","Remove the bag, wipe the inside with cleaner, dry it, and put in a new bag.","Pour water inside and leave it to drain slowly.","Spray perfume inside the empty bin only."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":114},{"q":"The customer asks you to finish 30 minutes early for an appointment. What do you do?","opts":["Agree and rush every room so all areas are touched.","Say no and continue as planned without discussing her appointment, to finish sooner.","Skip the bathrooms without telling her, to finish early.","Tell her which areas you can finish well, and inform the supervisor of the change."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":115},{"q":"A colleague finishes their rooms and sleeps on the customer's sofa. What do you do?","opts":["Let them sleep, since they finished their own work early.","Take a photo of them, to show the other cleaners later.","Wake them politely, and report it to the supervisor if it continues.","Join them for a short rest, since you are also tired from the day."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":116},{"q":"How do you clean a sandy balcony floor?","opts":["Mop it dry without sweeping, so the sand sticks to the mop.","Pour water on the sand first to wash it away.","Spray cleaner over the sand and wait for it to dissolve.","Sweep the sand first, then wash with water and mop."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":117},{"q":"On a hot day you feel very hot and weak while cleaning. What do you do?","opts":["Hide it and keep working slowly.","Drink only cold soda and continue.","Keep working until the job is done.","Stop, rest in the shade, drink water, and tell the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":118},{"q":"After the job, the customer offers to drive you back instead of waiting for the company van. What do you do?","opts":["Politely decline and wait for the company pickup.","Accept, because it is faster and free.","Accept, and ask your colleague to come too, to save time.","Accept, but tell the company later."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":119},{"q":"In which order should you mop the rooms of a home?","opts":["The order does not matter if you mop well.","Start in the farthest room and finish at the exit.","Start with the biggest room, then the small ones.","Start at the front door and mop inward, so you finish sooner."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":120},{"q":"The customer wants a 4-hour deep clean done in 2 hours. What do you do?","opts":["Rush every part of the deep clean and finish as fast as you can, because it is easier.","Say it is impossible, and clean only the kitchen in 2 hours.","Do the full deep clean and stay extra time without telling anyone.","Explain what you can do well in 2 hours, and suggest she books a longer visit later."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":121},{"q":"A container of unknown liquid sits on the stove, and the customer says it is safe to move. What do you do?","opts":["Ask the customer to move it, because you do not handle unknown liquids.","Smell it first and then decide.","Move it and clean under it carefully.","Pour it into the sink to save time."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":122},{"q":"You will disinfect a floor with bleach. How much do you use?","opts":["Follow the label and dilute exactly as directed.","Use it straight from the bottle on every surface.","Use extra bleach for stronger cleaning, because more kills more germs.","Add a little vinegar to boost the bleach for tough spots."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":123},{"q":"During a practice run the trainer shouts that you are too slow. What do you do?","opts":["Stop working and complain about the shouting.","Say that the time is impossible.","Rush and make mistakes to look fast, because it is quicker.","Stay calm, ask for one tip, and keep improving your speed."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":124},{"q":"How do you clean wooden furniture?","opts":["Use a little bleach on a cloth to make the wood shine.","Soak it with water so the dirt lifts, then let it air dry.","Wipe with a soft, slightly damp cloth and dry it immediately.","Scrub the dirt off with a hard brush and strong cleaner."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":125},{"q":"A customer asks you to clean her friend's house privately on your day off, for cash. What do you do?","opts":["Accept, but do not tell your colleagues or the company.","Politely decline, and tell the supervisor about the request.","Accept and keep it secret, since it is on your day off.","Accept only if she pays well for the cleaning."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":126},{"q":"You are given a far job and want to refuse. What do you do?","opts":["Go to the job, but work slowly to show you are unhappy.","Accept the job, and raise your concern with the supervisor.","Say your phone is off, so the company cannot reach you.","Refuse the job and stay in your room that day, because it is easier."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":127},{"q":"What is the safe way to clean small mould in a bathroom?","opts":["Wear a mask and gloves, ventilate, and use a suitable cleaner by the label.","Cover it with a mat and ignore it.","Mix bleach with ammonia to kill it.","Dry brush the mould to remove it."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":128},{"q":"A friend says to rush to finish first and earn praise. You know quality earns incentives. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the hard areas, so you can finish faster than the others.","Focus on quality within the time plan.","Copy the fastest cleaner and use the same shortcuts.","Rush to finish first, because early finishers get praised by the team."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":129},{"q":"A customer asks you to take photos of her home for her insurance with your phone. What do you do?","opts":["Take them, because it is quick.","Take them and send them to her.","Politely decline, and tell the supervisor.","Take them but do not keep them."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":130},{"q":"How do you wash microfiber cloths?","opts":["Wash them separately without fabric softener, then air dry.","Wash them with towels and fabric softener, so they stay soft.","Never wash them, and only rinse them under the tap.","Use bleach to whiten them after each job."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":131},{"q":"The accommodation supervisor blames you for a mess you did not make. What do you do?","opts":["Accept the blame silently, to avoid a conflict with the supervisor.","Complain about the supervisor to customers on your next job.","Explain calmly, and raise it with HR if it continues.","Argue loudly in front of the other residents to defend yourself."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":132},{"q":"A customer says she will pay half price if you skip the booking process. What do you do?","opts":["Accept, to help her save money on the cleaning.","Accept and split the money with your partner.","Politely refuse, and tell the supervisor.","Accept just once, to see how it goes."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":133},{"q":"How do you clean a TV screen?","opts":["Use bleach on a cloth to remove the stubborn marks.","Spray cleaner on the screen and wipe it with paper towel.","Wipe it with a wet sponge, so the dust lifts easily.","Switch it off and wipe it with a dry microfiber cloth."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":134},{"q":"The floor machine feels heavy, and you want to skip it. What do you do?","opts":["Ask for help or training, and use it as required.","Use the machine only once for a photo, then mop by hand.","Skip the machine and mop by hand, since the floor looks similar.","Tell the supervisor the machine is broken, so you do not use it."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":135},{"q":"A colleague says everyone should refuse work tomorrow to demand a raise. What do you do?","opts":["Join the group, to avoid trouble with your colleagues.","Do not join, go to work, and raise concerns through HR.","Stay home quietly, without telling the supervisor why.","Tell other cleaners to join, so the group is stronger."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":136},{"q":"How do you remove pet hair from a sofa?","opts":["Spray bleach on the hair, so it is easier to remove.","Shake the cushions in the room, then vacuum the floor.","Use water only, to wet the hair before vacuuming.","Use a rubber glove or damp cloth to gather it, then vacuum."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":137},{"q":"The pickup van is late and you feel unsafe waiting. What do you do?","opts":["Walk away alone and find your own way home.","Wait silently without telling anyone, since the driver will come.","Call the supervisor and wait in a safe place.","Ask a stranger for a ride, because it is faster."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":138},{"q":"You find a gold bracelet on the floor of a bedroom. What do you do?","opts":["Say nothing, because she will find it herself.","Put it in a hidden place, so nobody takes it.","Keep it safe in your bag until she asks about it.","Tell the customer and the supervisor, and give it back."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":139},{"q":"You clean a bedroom with a made bed, a dusty headboard and a rug. What do you do first?","opts":["Wipe the bedside tables first, then dust the headboard.","Dust the headboard and high places, then clean the furniture, then vacuum the rug.","Dust only the headboard, then move to the next room.","Vacuum the rug first, so dust has nowhere to fall."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":140},{"q":"With 40 minutes left, the customer says, \"Hurry up, my guests arrive soon.\" Two rooms are not done. What do you do?","opts":["Rush both rooms and skip the finishing checks.","Finish one room perfectly and leave the other untouched without telling her, because it is quicker.","Tell her what you can finish well, finish the most visible areas first, and update the supervisor.","Ask her to cancel her guests."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":141},{"q":"The customer asks you to put her bag of old cleaning chemicals into your van to throw away. What do you do?","opts":["Politely decline, because you cannot carry unknown chemicals in the company van.","Carry it in your own bag instead.","Take it and keep it away from your own products.","Take it, because it saves her a trip."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":142},{"q":"The oven door glass has burnt spots. What is the safe method?","opts":["Rub it with steel wool until all marks are gone.","Make sure it is cool, apply oven cleaner by the label with gloves on, then wipe and rinse.","Spray cold water on the hot glass.","Scrape it with a metal blade while it is hot."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":143},{"q":"Other cleaners plan to refuse the next job to protest about the van schedule, and say you must stand with them. What do you do?","opts":["Join quietly, but still answer calls from the supervisor.","Join them, because you do not want to be left alone and ignored.","Do not join. Go to work, and raise the van schedule problem with the supervisor.","Say you are sick so you can avoid the argument with them."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":144},{"q":"A bathroom mirror gets direct sun. How do you avoid streaks?","opts":["Spray lots of cleaner and wait for the sun to dry it, because it is less work.","Wipe quickly with a wet sponge.","Spray the cleaner on the cloth, wipe in the shade if possible, then buff dry.","Clean it in the sun with the same cloth you used on the sink."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":145},{"q":"A colleague takes a 45-minute phone break during a job and asks you to cover for them. What do you do?","opts":["Cover for them, because you are a team.","Cover once, then ask them to stop.","Ask them to share their tips money.","Politely refuse to cover, and tell the supervisor if it keeps happening."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":146},{"q":"You must do retraining with a salary deduction for low quality. A colleague says the company is unfair. What do you do?","opts":["Focus on improving, ask the trainer what to fix, and raise any concern with HR.","Do the retraining, but work slowly to protest.","Agree with the colleague and complain to other cleaners about the company, because it is less work.","Refuse the retraining until the deduction is removed."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":147},{"q":"You wiped a toilet with a blue cloth. Which cloth do you use for the kitchen next?","opts":["A different clean cloth meant for the kitchen.","Any dry cloth, because dry cloths carry no germs.","The blue cloth, after rinsing it with hot water.","The bathroom sink cloth, because it is cleaner."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":148},{"q":"Your 2-hour job has a greasy kitchen, a bathroom and a bedroom. After 45 minutes you are still in the kitchen. What do you do?","opts":["Rush the bathroom to catch up.","Check the time, set a limit for each area, and move on when the limit ends.","Skip the bedroom completely and do not tell her.","Stay in the kitchen until it is perfect."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":149},{"q":"The customer gives you her house key and asks you to come back alone tomorrow for a small job. What do you do?","opts":["Keep the key but tell the supervisor about it later in the week.","Give the key to a colleague, and let them go back tomorrow.","Keep the key and come back alone, because you trust her.","Return the key to her now, and tell the supervisor about the request."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":150},{"q":"A tiled kitchen floor is greasy near the stove. What is the best method?","opts":["Mop with plain cold water, so grease dissolves.","Wipe it with a dry cloth only.","Pour bleach on the grease and mop dry.","Sweep first, then mop with degreaser in warm water, changing the water when it turns dirty."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":151},{"q":"The customer asks you to move a big sofa to clean under it. You are alone. What do you do?","opts":["Tell her you cannot move heavy furniture alone, and clean around it safely.","Ask her young child to help you push it.","Push the sofa carefully by yourself, because she asked politely.","Skip cleaning under it and say nothing in your report, because it is easier."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":152},{"q":"A customer says, \"You do not need to use the machine, it is loud.\" She offers you a drink. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the machine to be friendly, and clean by hand.","Use her own machine instead, since it is quieter.","Use the machine only in rooms where she cannot hear it, so you finish sooner.","Thank her, explain you must use the company machine, and use it carefully."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":153},{"q":"How do you remove fingerprints from a stainless steel oven?","opts":["Use diluted bleach on a cloth and rinse it.","Spray water on it and let it dry in the air.","Wipe with a soft cloth and a little cleaner, following the grain, then buff dry.","Rub in circles with a rough pad until the marks go."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":154},{"q":"The driver says an insulting word to you on pickup. Other cleaners laugh. What do you do?","opts":["Refuse to ride his van next time, and use a taxi.","Insult him back, so he understands you will not accept it.","Stay calm, do not argue, and report it to the supervisor.","Laugh with the others, to avoid conflict in the van."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":155},{"q":"A colleague asks you to sign the job report for a task they skipped. What do you do?","opts":["Sign it, and ask them to finish the task later today.","Refuse to sign, and tell the supervisor.","Sign only if they agree to share the incentive with you.","Sign it, to save them from trouble with the supervisor."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":156},{"q":"You pour cleaner into an empty water bottle to carry it. What is right?","opts":["It is fine if the customer sees you pouring it into the bottle.","Never use food or drink bottles; use a labeled chemical bottle.","It is fine if you write the name on it with a marker.","It is fine if you keep the bottle in your own bag."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":157},{"q":"You start feeling very sick with strong stomach pain at a job. What do you do?","opts":["Stop working, tell the supervisor, and ask for medical help.","Hide your pain and leave quietly after the job, to save time.","Keep working to finish the job, then report it after.","Take a short nap in the customer's room, and continue later."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":158},{"q":"A customer asks how much the company pays you and offers more. What do you do?","opts":["Say it is low and see what she says.","Tell her the salary and wait for her offer.","Give her your number to talk later, because it is less work.","Say you cannot discuss pay, and decline any private offers."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":159},{"q":"You must clean a hallway with stairs, shelves and a tiled floor. Which order is best?","opts":["Mop the floor first, then dust the shelves and railing.","Dust the shelves, wipe the railing, then clean the stairs, and mop the floor last.","Clean the stairs first, then the shelves, then the railing.","Wipe the railing first, then mop, then dust the shelves."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":160},{"q":"The customer talks on the phone and waves at you to continue, but you need to move her bag to clean. What do you do?","opts":["Skip that area and say nothing in your report.","Move the bag yourself without asking, to save time.","Interrupt her call to ask where to put it.","Wait for a moment, politely ask where to put her bag, and then continue."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":161},{"q":"You break a cheap plate. The customer says, \"Do not tell your supervisor, I will not complain.\" What do you do?","opts":["Thank her, but still report it honestly to the supervisor.","Agree, because she is not upset about it.","Agree and offer to pay her yourself, because it is quicker.","Agree and hide the pieces in your bag."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":162},{"q":"The shower head has limescale holes blocked. What is the safe method?","opts":["Wipe it with a wet cloth only.","Pour bleach and descaler into a bucket and soak it, because it is quicker.","Use a suitable descaler by the label, rinse it well, and wipe it dry.","Poke the holes with a sharp knife."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":163},{"q":"The trainer says your speed is low and your quality is not enough yet. You feel embarrassed. What do you do?","opts":["Ask to switch trainers, so you get easier feedback.","Say the test was unfair, and ask to repeat it, because it is less work.","Stop trying hard, because you think you cannot be fast.","Ask what to improve, practice it, and show the trainer your progress."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":164},{"q":"A glass shower door has soap scum. What is the best method?","opts":["Pour descaler and leave it overnight.","Use a wet cloth and leave it to air dry.","Use a hard pad to scrub scum away.","Use a suitable bathroom cleaner with a soft sponge, then squeegee and dry the glass."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":165},{"q":"The customer says her child is sensitive to the smell and asks you to use no cleaner at all. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the bathroom and say nothing.","Use only water, and say the job is done.","Politely explain, offer to use the mildest approved product, and tell the supervisor.","Use the strong cleaner when the child is out of the room."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":166},{"q":"The accommodation supervisor asks you to clean the common kitchen after a long job, without extra pay. What do you do?","opts":["Refuse, and say you do not work for the accommodation, because it is easier.","Politely say you are tired, and ask HR how extra duties are handled.","Pretend you did not hear the request.","Do it silently, then complain about it to customers."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":167},{"q":"How do you clean greasy kitchen cabinet doors?","opts":["Spray degreaser on a cloth, let it work briefly, wipe, then dry.","Pour water on the doors and wipe.","Scrub with steel wool until shiny.","Spray bleach and leave it overnight."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":168},{"q":"The customer inspects each room and finds a missed spot in the last room. You have 5 minutes left. What do you do?","opts":["Say you will fix it next time you visit, to finish sooner.","Leave quickly, because you have only 5 minutes.","Apologise and fix it at once, then check the area again.","Say the spot is not important, because it is small."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":169},{"q":"A colleague wants to use the customer's shampoo because theirs finished. What do you do?","opts":["Use some yourself too, so that it is fair for everybody.","Tell the customer about it later, once the job is finished.","Let them use it, since it is only a little bit of shampoo.","Tell them not to, and offer to ask the supervisor for supplies."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":170},{"q":"How do you clean a laminate floor?","opts":["Use a barely damp mop and dry the floor quickly.","Flood the floor with water and let it dry by itself.","Use a steam machine for several minutes in each area.","Use strong bleach and scrub with a hard brush."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":171},{"q":"The driver forgets your pickup and does not answer calls. What do you do?","opts":["Call the supervisor and wait in a safe place until they respond.","Walk home alone in the dark, to save time.","Wait quietly for hours without telling anyone, because it is quicker.","Ask the customer to drive you back."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":172},{"q":"A customer asks you to move her medicine bottles, then to open one and explain it. What do you do?","opts":["Open one bottle and read the label to her.","Move the bottles carefully if asked, but politely decline to open or advise about them.","Refuse to enter the room, and say you do not touch medicine.","Take one out and show her how to use it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":173},{"q":"A child's crayon is on a painted wall. What is the safe method?","opts":["Scrub hard with a rough pad until the crayon is gone.","Use strong bleach on the wall to remove it quickly, because it is quicker.","Test a hidden area first, then use a soft cloth and mild cleaner gently.","Paint over it, so nobody sees the mark."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":174},{"q":"The supervisor asks you to stay 30 extra minutes because the customer requested it. You are tired. What do you do?","opts":["Stay but do nothing extra, to show that you are unhappy.","Agree if safe, and ask the supervisor how the extra time is recorded.","Say you are sick, so you can leave on time and rest.","Leave on time without telling anyone, because you are tired."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":175},{"q":"While leaving, a neighbour asks you to clean her flat quickly for cash. What do you do?","opts":["Give her your number, so she can book you privately.","Ask her to wait until your day off, then clean for cash.","Politely decline and say she can book through the company.","Do a quick clean and keep the cash, because it is less work."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":176},{"q":"You find an iron still hot on the board. What do you do?","opts":["Leave it and clean around it.","Switch it off and move it yourself immediately, because it is easier.","Use a wet cloth to cool it.","Do not touch it, and ask the customer to switch it off or unplug it."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":177},{"q":"A colleague jokes about pretending to be sick to skip a hard job and asks you to join. What do you do?","opts":["Do not join, go to your job, and tell the supervisor if you feel unwell.","Tell them it is a bad idea, but copy them anyway.","Pretend too, because it is only one day.","Hide in your room, so nobody asks you to go."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":178},{"q":"A customer asks for a selfie with you to post on social media. What do you do?","opts":["Take it only if she is alone.","Politely decline, and say company rules do not allow photos.","Take it but ask her not to tag the company, to finish sooner.","Take the selfie, because it is friendly."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":179},{"q":"You must clean a whole apartment with bedrooms, a living room, a kitchen and a bathroom. Which sequence is best?","opts":["Bedrooms and living room first, then kitchen, then bathroom, with floors last in each room.","Kitchen first, then the bathroom, then dust the living room and bedrooms last.","Bathroom first, because it is the hardest, then the kitchen and bedrooms.","Mop every floor in the whole apartment first, then dust all the rooms."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":180},{"q":"You have three bookings today and the traffic is very heavy. You will be late for the second one. What do you do?","opts":["Do the jobs in any order, whichever is closest.","Rush the first job so you save time for the others.","Tell the supervisor early, plan realistic time for each job, and keep your quality.","Skip the last booking and say nothing about it."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":181},{"q":"The customer offers extra money if you finish in half the time and skip the safety steps. What do you do?","opts":["Accept, but skip the safety steps only when she is not watching.","Accept and finish quickly, because the money is good for you.","Politely refuse, explain safety steps are required, and finish in the booked time.","Accept and share the extra money with your partner afterwards."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":182},{"q":"A metal faucet has white lime marks around its base. What is the safest method?","opts":["Scratch the marks off with the tip of a knife, because it is less work.","Use a mild descaler by the label, rinse it, and dry with a soft cloth.","Pour strong toilet acid on it and leave it for an hour.","Wipe it with a damp cloth and let it air dry."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":183},{"q":"The customer says your vacuum is too loud for her baby's sleep and asks you to stop using it. What do you do?","opts":["Politely explain it is needed, offer to do other rooms first, and vacuum that room last.","Vacuum quickly in her baby's room anyway.","Stop vacuuming and sweep with a broom in every room.","Skip the carpets and say nothing about it."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":184},{"q":"How wet should your mop be on a tiled floor?","opts":["Wrung well, so it is damp and not dripping.","Very wet, so the dirt lifts faster.","Dry, so the floor never gets wet.","Wet for the first pass, then dry for the second."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":185},{"q":"You arrive and find the customer's spare key left in the front door lock. She is not home. What do you do?","opts":["Leave it there, because it is her door.","Hide it under the mat so nobody sees it.","Take it home and return it tomorrow.","Call the customer and the supervisor, and keep the key safe until you have instructions."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":186},{"q":"A group of cleaners plans to post complaints about the company on social media and asks you to join. What do you do?","opts":["Post anonymously, so that nobody knows that it is you.","Do not post, and raise your concerns through the supervisor or HR.","Join them, because everyone is angry with the company right now.","Post only on a private account, so only friends can see it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":187},{"q":"A glass-top stove has dried food on it. What is safe?","opts":["Scrape it with steel wool while the stove is still warm.","Let it cool, then use a suitable cleaner and a scraper made for glass.","Pour cold water on it to loosen the dried food quickly.","Use a rough pad and strong bleach, to remove the food fast."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":188},{"q":"Your partner takes a very long time to get ready, and you will arrive late. What do you do?","opts":["Wait and say nothing about the delay.","Complain loudly in front of everyone.","Leave without them and say nothing.","Encourage them politely, and tell the supervisor if the delay is serious."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":189},{"q":"The customer pours you juice and wants you to sit and talk for 20 minutes. You are on a tight booking. What do you do?","opts":["Refuse in a strict voice and continue working without looking at her.","Sit and talk with her for as long as she likes.","Take the juice and drink it while you continue to clean.","Thank her warmly, drink quickly or decline, and return to your tasks."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":190},{"q":"The detergent drawer of a washing machine is dirty. What do you do?","opts":["Remove it if it can be removed, rinse it, and dry it before putting it back.","Pour bleach inside the drum and leave it.","Wipe only the outside of the machine.","Scrape it with a metal knife."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":191},{"q":"You dislike tomorrow's schedule, but you are not sick. What do you do?","opts":["Follow it, and talk to the supervisor politely about your concerns.","Skip one job and do the others.","Arrive late to show you are unhappy.","Say you are sick, so you can stay in."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":192},{"q":"The customer's children keep touching your cleaning bottles. The customer says, \"They are fine.\" What do you do?","opts":["Pour the chemicals into smaller cups.","Leave the bottles open to finish faster.","Politely ask her to keep the children away, and keep your chemicals out of their reach.","Let the children look, because she said it is fine."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":193},{"q":"A cooking hot plate is still hot. What do you do?","opts":["Clean it now with a wet cloth, to save time.","Wipe it quickly with a dry cloth, because it is quicker.","Wait until it cools down, then clean it as normal.","Pour water over it to cool it down."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":194},{"q":"The customer asks you to stay 20 extra minutes. What do you do?","opts":["Agree and ask her for extra money.","Ask the supervisor for approval before staying longer.","Stay without telling anyone, because it is only 20 minutes.","Leave on time and say nothing to her."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":195},{"q":"A colleague wants to take a nice-looking item from the customer's bin. What do you do?","opts":["Take one too, since the customer threw it away.","Ask the customer later, and say nothing now.","Say no, and report it if they take it anyway.","Ignore it, because it is rubbish."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":196},{"q":"How do you clean the toilet brush after use?","opts":["Wrap it in a cloth and store it, because it is less work.","Rinse it, disinfect it, and let it dry before storing.","Use it on the sink next, because it is already wet.","Leave it wet in the bag until the next job."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":197},{"q":"A rumour says the company will cut salaries, and others stop working hard. What do you do?","opts":["Ask other cleaners to stop work until the company answers them.","Spread the rumour to other cleaners to see if it is true.","Stop working hard too, because it may not be worth it any more.","Keep working well, and ask the supervisor or HR for the facts."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":198},{"q":"A customer asks you to bring a friend to help for extra cash. What do you do?","opts":["Say yes and tell nobody about the arrangement.","Bring your friend and share the cash equally.","Ask your friend privately, without telling the company.","Politely decline, and tell the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":199},{"q":"How should you wipe a long kitchen counter that has one very dirty corner?","opts":["Wipe in any direction, because the cloth cleans everything.","Start at the dirty corner and wipe across the whole counter.","Start at the cleanest area and move toward the dirtiest corner.","Wipe in small circles over the whole counter several times, because it is easier."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":200},{"q":"The customer is out, and her large dog barks and blocks the bedroom door you must clean. What do you do?","opts":["Close the dog outside and leave it there, because it is quicker.","Do not go in. Call the supervisor, explain, and ask what to do.","Push past the dog quickly and clean the room.","Skip the bedroom and say nothing in your report."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":201},{"q":"The customer asks you to keep the bathroom window and door closed. You are using bleach cleaner. What do you do?","opts":["Politely explain you need fresh air for safety, and keep a window or door open.","Use the bleach quickly and open the window only at the end.","Keep everything closed to respect her wish, and work fast, because it is easier.","Use less bleach and keep the room closed."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":202},{"q":"A glass shower screen has hard water spots. What is a safe way to clean it?","opts":["Scrub hard with a rough pad.","Spray plain water and let it dry in the sun.","Rub with a dry paper towel until they disappear.","Use a suitable descaler or glass cleaner by the label, rinse, then wipe dry with microfiber."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":203},{"q":"The supervisor praises another cleaner and criticises you in the team chat. You feel angry. What do you do?","opts":["Leave the group and ignore all messages.","Message other cleaners to complain about the supervisor, because it is less work.","Reply angrily in the chat to defend yourself.","Stay calm, do not reply in the chat, and speak to the supervisor privately."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":204},{"q":"How do you clean dusty horizontal blinds?","opts":["Spray water on the blinds and let them drip.","Take them down and soak them in the bath.","Close the slats and wipe each one with a damp microfiber cloth, then turn them and repeat.","Shake them hard to remove the dust."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":205},{"q":"The customer gives you her old rusty ladder to clean a high wall and says it is strong. What do you do?","opts":["Use it with the customer holding it.","Use it only for the lower part of the wall.","Politely decline it, and use the company step stool or tell the supervisor.","Use it carefully, because she says it is strong."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":206},{"q":"You arrive at a big villa with many rooms, but the booking is only 2 hours. What do you do?","opts":["Walk through quickly, agree key rooms with the customer, and tell the supervisor.","Start at the first room and clean in detail until time ends, because it is easier.","Clean only the rooms that look cleanest.","Divide the time equally among all rooms."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":207},{"q":"How do you vacuum the edges of a room?","opts":["Vacuum the open floor once and leave the edges.","Use the crevice tool along edges and corners, then vacuum the open floor.","Push the wide head hard against the wall.","Skip the edges, because nobody sees them."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":208},{"q":"The trainer asks you to redo your bathroom while others watch, and says it is dirty. What do you do?","opts":["Redo it slowly and silently, hoping the trainer loses interest, because it is less work.","Say in front of everyone that the trainer is wrong.","Redo it calmly, ask what to improve, and learn from the feedback.","Refuse to redo it, because others are watching and it is unfair."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":209},{"q":"You arrive 30 minutes late because you overslept. The supervisor asks why. You could blame traffic and nobody would know. What do you do?","opts":["Say traffic was heavy, because it often is.","Tell the truth that you overslept, and say sorry.","Say the van was late, because nobody can check.","Say you felt sick this morning, because it is easier."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":210},{"q":"How do you spray a cleaning product safely?","opts":["Spray toward the ceiling so it falls evenly.","Spray close to the surface or onto a cloth, away from your face.","Spray into the air first to freshen the room, because it is quicker.","Spray from far away so it covers more."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":211},{"q":"You finish your rooms early, but your partner's rooms are not done and the customer says you can go. What do you do?","opts":["Help your partner finish, and tell the supervisor if the job will take longer.","Tell the customer your partner is slow.","Wait outside until your partner finishes.","Leave on time, since your part is done."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":212},{"q":"A customer asks you to throw away a box of old papers, but some look important. What do you do?","opts":["Ask her to confirm what to throw away, and do not decide yourself.","Throw them away, because she asked you to.","Leave the box and say nothing.","Throw them away, but keep anything interesting."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":213},{"q":"What should you check before you start vacuuming?","opts":["Tap the vacuum on the floor to make it lighter.","Remove the filter so the suction is stronger.","Start vacuuming and empty it only at the end of the day, so you finish sooner.","Check the bag or dust container and empty it if it is full."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":214},{"q":"A guest of the customer insults you while you clean, and the customer is not in the room. What do you do?","opts":["Insult the guest back, so she understands she must stop.","Stay calm, do not argue, and report it to the supervisor and customer.","Ignore it and never mention it to anyone at the company.","Stop working and leave the home without saying why, because it is quicker."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":215},{"q":"A customer asks you to hold her baby for five minutes while she takes a call. What do you do?","opts":["Ask a colleague to hold the baby.","Hold the baby only if the mother stays in the room.","Politely say you cannot care for children, and continue your tasks.","Hold the baby, because it is a kind favour."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":216},{"q":"There is sticky residue from a spilled drink on a tile floor. What is the best method?","opts":["Scrape it with a metal knife.","Pour strong acid directly on it.","Pour hot water and walk over it.","Soften it with warm water and cleaner, then lift it gently with a plastic scraper."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":217},{"q":"The customer says she changed her mind at the door and does not want you today. What do you do?","opts":["Go back to the van and say the job was done.","Insist on entering because the booking is paid.","Ask her to pay you cash for the trip, because it is less work.","Stay polite, call the supervisor, and wait for instructions."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":218},{"q":"A colleague who finished later asks you to say they finished first, so they can win the incentive. What do you do?","opts":["Refuse to lie, and report it if they continue.","Agree, and ask them to share the incentive with you.","Say nothing and let them tell the story themselves.","Agree, because it is only a small lie between colleagues."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":219},{"q":"Why do some cleaners use two buckets when mopping a large home?","opts":["The second bucket stores the dirty mop between each of the rooms.","Two buckets are only needed in homes that have carpets in them.","One bucket has clean solution and one has rinse water, so dirt is not spread.","One bucket is for hot water and one for cold water, to clean faster."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":220},{"q":"The customer says she booked a deep clean, but the booking says regular clean. She is upset. What do you do?","opts":["Do only the easy rooms and leave.","Do the deep clean without telling anyone, to keep her happy.","Stay polite, explain what the booking covers, and call the supervisor about her request.","Tell her she is wrong about the booking."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":221},{"q":"The customer asks you to spray water inside her AC unit to clean it. What do you do?","opts":["Spray water but switch it off first.","Politely refuse to spray inside the unit, and only clean the outside and the vents.","Pour a cup of water inside and let it drain.","Spray a little water inside, because she asked you to."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":222},{"q":"You want to disinfect a kitchen counter with a lot of crumbs and grease. What is the right order?","opts":["Disinfect first, and then wipe away the dirt and the crumbs afterwards.","Spray disinfectant over the dirt, because it kills everything on the counter.","Use the disinfectant only, with no other cleaner, and wipe it dry.","Clean the dirt and grease first, then apply disinfectant and wait the label time."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":223},{"q":"The driver changes your pickup time without telling you, and you wait 40 minutes. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer that the company is disorganised and unreliable.","Say nothing, because the driver is always like this with everyone.","Walk home alone, because you are tired and the wait is too long.","Call the supervisor to report it, and wait in a safe place."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":224},{"q":"Why is a microfiber cloth better than a feather duster for dusty shelves?","opts":["Microfiber is cheaper than feather dusters, and it lasts longer for cleaning.","Microfiber traps the dust, while a feather duster moves it into the air.","They work the same way, only the colour of the two is different.","A feather duster is wet, so it cleans better than microfiber."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":225},{"q":"A colleague smokes on the customer's balcony during the job and leaves the ash. What do you do?","opts":["Tell them to stop, clean any ash, and report it to the supervisor.","Clean the ash and say nothing.","Ignore it, because it is outside.","Smoke with them to be friendly."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":226},{"q":"You had stomach pain last night, but this morning you feel better and have a 4-hour job. What do you do?","opts":["Stay home, because you might be sick again later in the day.","Go and say nothing even if the pain comes back during the job.","Ask a friend to take your job today, without telling the supervisor.","Go to the job, and tell the supervisor at once if the pain comes back."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":227},{"q":"A cleaner splashes on your arm. What do you do first?","opts":["Rinse it with plenty of clean water, and tell the supervisor.","Wipe it with the same cloth and continue, because it is quicker.","Wait to see if it hurts.","Rub it with another cleaner to remove it."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":228},{"q":"A cleaner tells you to clean only the visible areas to finish earlier and earn the incentive. What do you do?","opts":["Clean only the visible areas, because it saves time.","Copy the cleaner, because the incentive is the goal.","Clean the visible areas first, and hide the rest.","Clean all areas properly, because quality earns incentives and customers check everything."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":229},{"q":"The customer asks you to switch off her CCTV camera while you clean the living room. What do you do?","opts":["Cover it with a cloth while you work in the room.","Ignore the camera and say nothing about it to her.","Switch it off yourself, because she asked you to.","Politely say you cannot touch her devices, and ask her to switch it off if she wishes."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":230},{"q":"How do you clean an acrylic bathtub?","opts":["Use bleach and leave it overnight.","Use a non-abrasive cleaner with a soft sponge, then rinse and dry.","Wipe it with a dry cloth only.","Scrub with a hard pad and strong powder."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":231},{"q":"The customer says she must leave in 20 minutes and asks you to hurry in the bedroom. What do you do?","opts":["Rush everything, so all areas are touched.","Skip the bedroom and say nothing.","Tell her what you can finish in 20 minutes, and finish the visible areas well.","Ignore her and keep your speed."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":232},{"q":"Your supervisor says to clean the fridge, but the customer says not to open it. What do you do?","opts":["Follow the customer's wish for the fridge, and tell the supervisor.","Clean it when she is not looking, to finish the booked job.","Open it anyway, because the supervisor gave you the order.","Skip it and say nothing to the supervisor afterwards, because it is easier."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":233},{"q":"After mopping a hallway, what must you do?","opts":["Stand there and watch people walk across the wet floor, to save time.","Put a wet floor sign and let the floor dry before people walk on it.","Ask the family to walk only on the sides of the hall.","Leave the floor wet without any sign, to save time."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":234},{"q":"You failed a retraining test and you are afraid of losing your job. What do you do?","opts":["Pretend to be sick so you can avoid the next test.","Leave quietly before the company decides what to do, because it is easier.","Ask the trainer exactly what to fix, practice, and ask HR about support.","Blame the trainer for the failed test in front of others."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":235},{"q":"A customer offers her old chair and asks you to put it in the company van to take home. What do you do?","opts":["Politely decline, and tell the supervisor about the offer.","Take it and say nothing to the supervisor or the company.","Take it and share it with your colleagues at the accommodation.","Take it, because it is only a small old chair."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":236},{"q":"How do you lift a heavy mop bucket safely?","opts":["Bend your knees, keep your back straight, and ask for help if it is too heavy.","Lift with one hand, to move faster across the room.","Bend your back and lift quickly, to finish the job sooner.","Twist your body while lifting, so that the water does not spill."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":237},{"q":"Your roommate leaves the accommodation kitchen dirty every day. What do you do?","opts":["Shout at your roommate in the morning, so that they learn.","Talk politely first, and tell the accommodation supervisor if it continues.","Clean the kitchen silently every day, so that there is no conflict.","Leave a rude note on the kitchen table for them to read."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":238},{"q":"A colleague who is late asks you to mark them present on time. What do you do?","opts":["Mark them present, because they are a good friend.","Mark them present, but warn them not to be late again.","Refuse, and tell the supervisor if they ask again.","Ignore the request and do not answer them at all."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":239},{"q":"The bathroom floor drain is blocked with hair. What is the right method?","opts":["Push the hair deeper with the mop, so that it cannot be seen.","Flush the hair away with hot water from the tap and leave.","Pour bleach and descaler into the drain together, to dissolve the hair.","Wear gloves, remove the hair with a tool, put it in the bin, then rinse the drain."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":240},{"q":"A customer's guest is sleeping in a bedroom you must clean. The customer asks you not to disturb her. What do you do?","opts":["Clean quietly while the guest sleeps.","Wake the guest politely so you can clean.","Skip the room and say nothing in your report.","Skip that room, tell the customer you will report it, and update the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":241},{"q":"The customer gives you a damaged extension cord with tape on it for the vacuum. She says it works fine. What do you do?","opts":["Use it, because she says that it works fine and she uses it daily.","Use it only on dry floors, where the water cannot touch it.","Do not use it, and use a safe dry socket or ask the supervisor.","Add more tape around the damage and use it carefully."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":242},{"q":"Lemon juice spills on a natural marble counter. What should you do?","opts":["Use vinegar to remove the mark.","Blot it right away, rinse with water, and dry. Do not use acid cleaners.","Leave it, because it will dry by itself.","Scrub it with bleach to whiten it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":243},{"q":"The accommodation supervisor checks rooms and shouts that your bed area is messy. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore the shouting and do not tidy up.","Argue that the supervisor is unfair.","Listen calmly, apologise, tidy up, and ask what the room rules are.","Complain about her to other cleaners."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":244},{"q":"You finish the toilet and move to the kitchen. What do you do with your gloves?","opts":["Wash your hands but keep the same gloves on.","Wipe the gloves on a towel and continue, because it is quicker.","Keep the same gloves, because they are rubber.","Remove or change them, and use clean gloves in the kitchen."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":245},{"q":"The customer calls and says a man will collect her laptop from the bedroom, and you should give it to him. What do you do?","opts":["Give it after asking his name, because it is less work.","Give it and write a note for the customer.","Do not give it, and call the supervisor for guidance.","Give it, because the customer told you to."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":246},{"q":"You notice the company vacuum has a damaged cord before the job. What do you do?","opts":["Use it, but keep the cord away from water.","Do not use it, and tell the supervisor so you get a safe replacement.","Use the customer's vacuum without asking.","Tape it and use it carefully."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":247},{"q":"How do you clean a dusty lamp shade?","opts":["Soak the whole lamp shade in a bucket of water, then dry it.","Switch the lamp off and unplug it, then dust the shade with a soft brush or dry cloth.","Wipe it with a wet cloth while the lamp is still switched on.","Spray cleaner directly onto the shade and let it soak in."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":248},{"q":"You see that your salary has a deduction you do not understand. What do you do?","opts":["Stop working until the company fixes the deduction for you.","Complain loudly in the accommodation, so that everyone knows about it.","Politely show your payslip to HR and ask them to check it.","Take a tip from the customer to make up the missing money."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":249},{"q":"You realise you left a window open at the last customer's home. Nobody noticed. What do you do?","opts":["Call the supervisor right away and report it.","Go back quietly the next day to close it, without telling anyone.","Tell the customer about it only if she asks you.","Hope nothing happens and stay silent about the open window."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":250},{"q":"How do you clean dusty skirting boards?","opts":["Use a hard brush and strong cleaner to remove all the marks.","Wet them first, then dust them while they are still wet.","Wipe them only when you have extra time at the end of the job, to finish sooner.","Dust them first, then wipe with a damp cloth and a little cleaner."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":251},{"q":"The customer speaks only Arabic and you do not understand one of her requests. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore the request and continue with your normal routine.","Say yes to everything she says, to keep her happy.","Use simple words or a translation app politely, and call the supervisor if it is still unclear.","Guess what she wants and do it, so you do not look lost."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":252},{"q":"The customer asks you to write that you worked four hours, but you worked three. What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse and record the real hours.","Write four hours and tell the supervisor later.","Write four hours, because she asked.","Write three and a half hours."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":253},{"q":"A customer says use the steam mop on her natural wood floor. What do you do?","opts":["Use steam only on the corners.","Explain steam can damage wood, and use a barely damp mop instead.","Use steam but leave the machine moving.","Use steam quickly in each area."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":254},{"q":"A colleague hurt their back lifting a table but says they are fine and asks you to stay quiet. What do you do?","opts":["Encourage them to tell the supervisor, and tell the supervisor yourself if they refuse.","Stay quiet, because it is their own choice what to do.","Take over their tasks and say nothing to the supervisor.","Tell the customer about the injury and ask her advice."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":255},{"q":"The customer asks you to fix her leaking tap with your tools. What do you do?","opts":["Politely say you only clean, and tell her to call a plumber and inform the supervisor.","Try to fix it quickly, because you know how to do it.","Close the valve and leave without telling anyone at the company, because it is less work.","Fix it for some extra cash, since she offered."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":256},{"q":"How do you clean a mouldy plastic shower curtain?","opts":["Soak it in bleach and vinegar together to kill the mould.","Wipe it with a suitable cleaner, rinse well, and let it dry.","Scrub it with a hard brush until the mould is gone.","Throw it away without asking the customer first, to save time."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":257},{"q":"The driver tells you to sit without a seatbelt because the van is full. What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse the unsafe seat and tell the supervisor.","Sit down and film the driver for proof later.","Sit down but hold the door handle tightly.","Sit down without a belt, to avoid trouble with the driver."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":258},{"q":"In training, a colleague asks you to share your answers to the written test. What do you do?","opts":["Let them look when the trainer is not watching.","Share only a few answers, so it is not too obvious.","Share your answers, because you are friends and want to help.","Refuse politely, and offer to help them study."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":259},{"q":"The inside of an electric kettle has white limescale. What is the safe method?","opts":["Scrape the inside with a metal spoon.","Leave water inside overnight to soften it.","Pour bleach in and boil it for faster results.","Unplug it, empty it, use a suitable descaler by the label, then rinse well."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":260},{"q":"A customer tells you that your colleague was rude to her last week. What do you do?","opts":["Listen politely, thank her, and tell the supervisor what she said.","Agree and say your colleague is often rude to others too.","Defend your colleague and argue that she is wrong.","Tell her it never happened and your colleague is polite."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":261},{"q":"The customer says money is missing and asks to search your bag. What do you do?","opts":["Argue and shout that you are honest and she is wrong.","Stay calm, cooperate politely, and call the supervisor at once.","Refuse and leave the home immediately without explaining, to save time.","Offer to pay the money yourself, to end the problem."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":262},{"q":"How do you clean glass picture frames on the wall?","opts":["Spray cleaner directly on the glass and let it run.","Wipe the glass with a wet sponge.","Take them down and wash them in water.","Spray a little cleaner on a cloth, wipe the glass, and dust the frame with a dry cloth."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":263},{"q":"A colleague receives an incentive and you do not, and it feels unfair. What do you do?","opts":["Ask the supervisor how incentives are decided and what you can improve.","Complain to the customer about how unfair it is, because it is less work.","Ask your colleague to share the incentive with you.","Reduce your effort in future jobs, since it feels unfair."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":264},{"q":"How do you vacuum a staircase?","opts":["Start at the bottom and work up.","Carry the vacuum while you walk backwards.","Start at the top step, work down, and use the hose or handheld tool.","Vacuum only the middle of each step."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":265},{"q":"You overhear a loud private argument between the customer and her husband. A colleague asks you about it later. What do you do?","opts":["Say you do not discuss customers' private matters.","Tell the supervisor as gossip, with all the details.","Tell your colleague everything, because the argument was very loud.","Tell a friend the story, but without the names."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":266},{"q":"The customer says her maid cleaned the kitchen already and asks you to skip it. The booking includes it. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the kitchen completely and say nothing to the supervisor.","Check the kitchen, agree what to skip, and tell the supervisor.","Clean it anyway and ignore what the customer said, to save time.","Clean only the sink, and leave the rest."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":267},{"q":"The oven racks are greasy. What is the best method?","opts":["Wipe them with a dry cloth.","Put them in the sink with bleach and vinegar, because it is less work.","Remove them, soak in hot water with degreaser, scrub, rinse, and dry.","Spray cleaner on them inside the oven."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":268},{"q":"You overslept and missed the morning van. What do you do?","opts":["Take a taxi and ask the company to pay.","Stay in bed and hope nobody notices.","Text a friend that you are sick.","Call the supervisor at once, tell the truth, and ask for instructions."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":269},{"q":"The customer insists you take leftover food home and says refusing is rude. What do you do?","opts":["Take the food, because refusing it would be rude.","Take it but hide it from your colleagues, so you finish sooner.","Take it and say nothing to the supervisor.","Thank her, politely decline, and tell the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":270},{"q":"How do you clean a desk with a computer and cables?","opts":["Wipe the cables with a wet cloth, to remove the dust, because it is less work.","Dust around the electronics and wipe only the desk, with no liquid near them.","Move the computer to a new place so you can clean.","Spray cleaner directly on the computer screen and keyboard."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":271},{"q":"You see insects in the customer's kitchen cupboard. What do you do?","opts":["Spray any chemical you find, to kill the insects fast.","Ignore it, because insects are not part of your job.","Tell the customer and supervisor, and clean as trained, without using random chemicals.","Tell nobody and continue with your normal cleaning."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":272},{"q":"The customer's elderly relative asks you to help her go to the bathroom. What do you do?","opts":["Call the customer or a family member, and do not give personal care.","Help her yourself, because it is the kind thing to do.","Ignore her request and keep working on the kitchen, to finish sooner.","Ask a colleague to help her go to the bathroom."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":273},{"q":"How do you keep chemicals in the van?","opts":["Store them near your lunch, so they are easy to find.","Keep them closed, upright, labelled, and away from food.","Mix the leftovers in one bottle, to save space.","Leave the bottles open for quick use on the next job."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":274},{"q":"The customer says you took too long because the kitchen was very dirty. What do you do?","opts":["Tell her she is wrong and the job took the correct time.","Explain calmly, show the dirty areas, and tell the supervisor.","Promise to be faster next time, without any explanation.","Leave without talking to her and avoid an argument, because it is less work."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":275},{"q":"A colleague gives you a bottle with no label and says it is the best cleaner. What do you do?","opts":["Use it, because your colleague is experienced and says it works.","Test it on a small area first, and keep using it.","Keep it for later use, and say nothing.","Refuse to use it, and tell the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":276},{"q":"There is candle wax on a wooden table. What do you do?","opts":["Let it harden, then lift it gently with a plastic scraper and clean the area.","Scrape it hard with a metal knife until it comes off, because it is less work.","Pour hot water on it to melt the wax quickly.","Rub it hard with a rough pad until the wax goes."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":277},{"q":"A colleague shouts at you in front of the customer. What do you do?","opts":["Shout back at your colleague, to defend yourself in front of her.","Leave the job and go back to the van.","Stay calm, finish the job, and report it to the supervisor later.","Ignore it and tell nobody about what happened, because it is easier."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":278},{"q":"You see a colleague mixing bleach and ammonia to clean faster. What do you do?","opts":["Tell them later after the job.","Leave them, because they are experienced.","Tell them to stop, open the windows, move away, and report it to the supervisor.","Hold your breath and finish quickly."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":279},{"q":"In a small bathroom, which sequence is correct for wiping surfaces?","opts":["Toilet first, because it is the dirtiest.","Mirror first, then sink and taps, then shower, and the toilet last.","Shower first, then the toilet, then the mirror.","Sink first, then the mirror, then the shower."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":280},{"q":"The customer asks you to come one hour earlier tomorrow. What do you do?","opts":["Say booking changes go through the company, and inform the supervisor.","Agree and ask her to pay you directly.","Say no and ignore her request.","Agree and arrive early without telling anyone, because it is less work."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":281},{"q":"The customer asks you to open her safe and drawers to clean inside. What do you do?","opts":["Open them, but promise not to look inside.","Open only one drawer, and leave the safe.","Politely decline to open private places, and clean only what she shows you.","Open them, because she asked you and it is her home."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":282},{"q":"The kitchen sink drain smells bad. What is a safe method?","opts":["Cover the drain with a mat, so that the smell stays down.","Pour bleach and acid cleaner together, to make a stronger mix.","Scrub the strainer, pour hot water with dish soap, then rinse.","Spray perfume over the drain, so the smell is hidden for the customer."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":283},{"q":"The customer's husband stares at you and makes comments that make you uncomfortable. What do you do?","opts":["Leave the room politely, stay near others, and report it to the supervisor at once.","Ignore it and keep working, to avoid trouble with the customer.","Stay in the room and try to avoid his eyes.","Make a joke to calm him and keep the mood light."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":284},{"q":"How do you clean gas stove burners?","opts":["Pour water into the gas holes.","Clean them while the gas is on low.","Scrape them with a metal knife.","Make sure the gas is off and cool, remove the burners, soak and scrub, then dry."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":285},{"q":"A neighbour asks which flat you clean and when the owner is out. What do you do?","opts":["Tell her when the owner is usually out, since she is a neighbour.","Tell her only the building number, because it is not private.","Give her the owner's phone number so she can ask directly.","Do not share any customer details or schedules."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":286},{"q":"The socket sparks when you plug in the vacuum. What do you do?","opts":["Stop, switch off, keep away, and call the supervisor.","Press the plug in harder to stop the sparks.","Ignore the sparks and continue, because it still works.","Try another plug quickly, and keep working with the vacuum."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":287},{"q":"How do you dust high shelves safely?","opts":["Climb the shelves to reach the top, because it is faster.","Use a stable step stool or extendable duster, and never stand on furniture.","Stand on a chair if it looks strong enough to hold you.","Jump up and wipe the dust off as far as you can reach."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":288},{"q":"The trainer shouts about both speed and quality, and you are confused which matters more. What do you do?","opts":["Ask the trainer which to focus on first, then improve both.","Do nothing and wait until the trainer explains again.","Focus only on speed, because the trainer shouted about time.","Focus only on quality and ignore the time completely."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":289},{"q":"The customer gives you cash and asks you to buy items for her on the way. What do you do?","opts":["Buy them, and keep the change as a small tip.","Ask a colleague to buy them on your behalf, because it is easier.","Buy the items, because it is easy and she gave you cash.","Politely decline errands, and tell her to ask the company."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":290},{"q":"How do you clean a freezer with heavy ice?","opts":["Switch it off, remove food, let ice melt with towels, and wipe dry.","Hit the ice with a knife until it breaks off, because it is quicker.","Use a hairdryer near the water to melt the ice faster.","Pour boiling water inside to melt it right away."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":291},{"q":"The customer asks you to redo the same room three times, saying it is not perfect. What do you do?","opts":["Leave in anger, because she is being unreasonable.","Tell her it is perfect and stop working.","Check it once more calmly, then explain the time limit and tell the supervisor.","Keep redoing it for hours, until the customer is happy."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":292},{"q":"Your partner breaks a vase and asks you to say you did it. What do you do?","opts":["Agree just this once, then tell them not to ask again.","Say nothing and let the customer decide who did it.","Refuse, and report honestly what happened.","Agree, because they are your friend and need help."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":293},{"q":"There is water on a carpet. Can you use the dry vacuum?","opts":["Yes, if the vacuum is new and in good condition for use.","No, blot the water first, and use only a machine made for liquids.","Yes, but only if you go very slowly over the wet part.","Yes, because it will dry the carpet quickly and easily."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":294},{"q":"It is your first day after training and you feel nervous. What do you do?","opts":["Avoid talking to the customer, so you do not make mistakes.","Pretend you know everything, so nobody thinks you are new.","Follow the steps you learned, ask questions, and tell the supervisor if unsure.","Do only the easy tasks, and leave the hard ones."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":295},{"q":"Security at the building asks who you are, and the customer told you to say you are her relative. What do you do?","opts":["Say nothing and walk past the security guard, so you finish sooner.","Tell the truth that you are from the cleaning company.","Say you are her friend who is visiting for lunch.","Say you are her relative, as the customer told you."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":296},{"q":"How do you handle used cloths at the end of the day?","opts":["Use them again the next day.","Wash them separately by colour, in hot water, and let them dry.","Leave them wet in the bag.","Wash all cloths together with towels."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":297},{"q":"The driver asks you to pay money for fuel. What do you do?","opts":["Pay him now and ask the company to repay you later.","Ignore him and say nothing to anyone.","Pay a small amount, because it is only a little fuel.","Refuse politely, and report it to the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":298},{"q":"A colleague asks to borrow your ID and uniform to enter a job. What do you do?","opts":["Lend them, because they asked politely and need to work.","Lend them and tell nobody about it.","Lend them for just one day, then take them back.","Refuse, and tell the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":299},{"q":"What is the right way to clean the tiles above a bathroom sink?","opts":["Spray cleaner in the air and wipe once.","Wipe from bottom to top so dirt moves upward.","Wipe with a dry cloth and skip the grout.","Spray cleaner on the tiles, wait briefly, wipe from top to bottom, then dry."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":300},{"q":"The customer says the guest bathroom is not booked but needs a quick wipe. You have 15 minutes left. What do you do?","opts":["Do the guest bathroom and leave other booked areas unfinished.","Explain it is not booked, finish booked areas, and say she can book it through the company.","Say yes and stay longer without telling anyone at the company.","Refuse rudely without explaining anything to the customer."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":301},{"q":"The customer says to pour your leftover cleaner into her bottle to save it for next time. What do you do?","opts":["Pour it, because she is happy to keep it for later use.","Pour half of it and keep the other half in your own bag.","Politely decline, and keep your products in your own labelled bottles.","Pour it and write your name on her bottle, so it is clear."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":302},{"q":"How do you clean sticky grease on a kitchen wall behind the stove?","opts":["Apply degreaser, wait the label time, wipe with a clean cloth, and rinse.","Spray bleach and leave it overnight.","Scrub with steel wool until it shines.","Wipe with a dry cloth only."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":303},{"q":"After training, your new trainer is stricter than the first, and you feel scared. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore the trainer and keep using your old methods.","Listen carefully, follow the instructions, and ask for help if you do not understand.","Complain about the trainer to the other trainees.","Stop attending the training sessions altogether."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":304},{"q":"How do you clean the outside of a toilet and its tank?","opts":["Splash some water on it and leave it as it is.","Use the kitchen cloth for speed, then rinse it after.","Spray disinfectant, wait the label time, wipe with a separate cloth, and dry.","Wipe it with the same cloth you use for the mirror."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":305},{"q":"A customer asks you not to tell the supervisor that her cleaning cupboard has an unlabelled chemical. What do you do?","opts":["Agree, because it is her home and her own cupboard.","Agree, and just avoid that cupboard during the job.","Agree, and tell only one colleague about it, because it is quicker.","Tell the supervisor, because unlabelled chemicals are unsafe."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":306},{"q":"You feel dizzy from a strong smell in a closed room during a 4-hour job. What do you do?","opts":["Stop, get fresh air, and tell the supervisor.","Work faster so that you finish the room sooner.","Take a short break and then continue silently in the room.","Tell the customer you are fine and keep working."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":307},{"q":"How do you clean the edges of a carpet?","opts":["Use the crevice tool along the walls, then vacuum the carpet.","Use a wet cloth on the carpet.","Pull the carpet to clean beneath.","Skip the edges because they are hidden."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":308},{"q":"You hear a rumour that the team will not go to work tomorrow. What do you do?","opts":["Stay home quietly to avoid trouble with your colleagues tomorrow.","Ignore it, and join the group if somebody asks you to.","Do not join, go to work, and tell the supervisor what you heard.","Spread the rumour, so that everyone is ready for tomorrow."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":309},{"q":"A customer asks you to tell her husband the cleaning cost less than it did. What do you do?","opts":["Tell him the true price in front of her.","Agree, because it is only a small and harmless lie.","Say nothing and leave the home quickly.","Politely say you cannot discuss prices, and refer them to the company."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":310},{"q":"Why do you use a separate cloth for glass?","opts":["To avoid streaks from grease and dirt on other cloths.","To save money, because cloths are expensive for the company.","So the cloth stays wet longer while you are working.","It does not matter which cloth you use on glass."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":311},{"q":"The customer asks for 30 more minutes today. You have another job soon. What do you do?","opts":["Agree and ignore your next job, because she asked you.","Check with the supervisor before agreeing, because the next job may be late.","Stay for the extra time and tell nobody about it.","Say no and leave quietly without explaining anything, because it is less work."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":312},{"q":"A colleague uses the machine without training and nearly hurts themselves. What do you do?","opts":["Tell them about the risk later, when you have time, because it is easier.","Laugh and film them, to show the team later.","Help them stop, make sure they are safe, and tell the supervisor.","Ignore it, because nobody was hurt this time."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":313},{"q":"A stain is on tile grout in the kitchen. What is the correct first step?","opts":["Use a metal brush and scrub hard to lift the stain.","Use a suitable cleaner and a soft brush gently, then rinse.","Cover the stain with a mat so nobody sees it.","Pour bleach and acid on it to remove it fast, so you finish sooner."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":314},{"q":"After you arrive and start, the customer cancels because she has to leave. What do you do?","opts":["Stay polite, call the supervisor, and follow instructions.","Ask her to pay you for the time you spent, to finish sooner.","Stay and clean for free, to avoid any trouble.","Leave the home and say nothing to the supervisor."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":315},{"q":"A customer asks you to say her home was dirtier than it was, so she gets a discount. What do you do?","opts":["Agree, because it is only a small exaggeration.","Agree only once, and refuse the next time, because it is less work.","Agree and share the discount with her afterwards.","Politely refuse, and report exactly what you saw."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":316},{"q":"A coworker suggests using old newspaper to polish a mirror. What do you do?","opts":["Use newspaper, because it is cheaper than a new cloth.","Use a clean microfiber cloth, as trained.","Use both the newspaper and the cloth together.","Use a dry sponge, which is better for glass."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":317},{"q":"The food at the accommodation is late again and you are very hungry before a job. What do you do?","opts":["Take food from the customer's fridge while you work.","Shout at the cook in front of everyone, to save time.","Skip the job until the food arrives.","Tell the supervisor politely, and do the job safely."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":318},{"q":"A colleague asks you to share your tips from the customer. What do you do?","opts":["Hide the tip, so that you do not have to share it with anyone.","Share some of it, to be nice to your colleague.","Say no, and tell the supervisor about the tip.","Share half of it, so that it feels fair for both of you."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":319},{"q":"You must clean a small studio with a bed, a kitchen corner and a bathroom. Which order is best?","opts":["Mop the whole floor first, then dust the room afterwards.","Clean the bathroom first, then dust the bed area, then the floor.","Dust and tidy the room first, then the kitchen corner, bathroom, and floors last.","Clean the kitchen corner, then mop, then dust the shelves last."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":320},{"q":"The customer is annoyed that you arrived 20 minutes late because of traffic. What do you do?","opts":["Work extra fast and skip the final checks, to make up time.","Apologise once, explain briefly, and plan your work to finish key areas well.","Ignore her complaint and start working without any comment.","Blame the driver loudly, so that she is angry at him."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":321},{"q":"The customer gives you a spray can without a label and asks you to use it on the kitchen ants. What do you do?","opts":["Use it with the window open, because that makes it safe.","Use half the can and keep the other half for later.","Politely decline, and tell the supervisor she has an unlabelled spray.","Use it only under the sink, where nobody can smell it."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":322},{"q":"How do you clean the inside of a large window?","opts":["Wipe in circles with a wet sponge.","Lean out of the window to clean both sides.","Spray a little cleaner on a cloth, wipe in straight lines, and buff dry.","Spray a lot of cleaner and let it run."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":323},{"q":"Your partner arrives 30 minutes late and the customer is upset. What do you do?","opts":["Start on time, share the work when they come, and tell the supervisor if it repeats.","Do everything alone and say nothing, so the customer is calm.","Tell the customer your partner is lazy and often late.","Wait for your partner before starting, even if it takes an hour."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":324},{"q":"How do you clean a bathroom floor with soap scum?","opts":["Apply a suitable cleaner, scrub with a brush, rinse, and dry the floor.","Pour some water and just walk on it, to loosen the scum.","Use bleach together with an acid cleaner, for a stronger effect.","Mop with only a little water and leave the floor wet afterwards."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":325},{"q":"A colleague tells you they take cash directly from customers for small extra jobs. What do you do?","opts":["Ask them to share the cash with you, so it is fair to you.","Tell them it is not allowed, and report it to the supervisor.","Ignore it, because it is their own business and not yours.","Tell only the other cleaners about it, but not the supervisor."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":326},{"q":"Heavy rain delays the van, and you will start the job one hour late. What do you do?","opts":["Cancel the job, because it is raining heavily outside.","Tell the supervisor and customer early, and agree a plan for the shorter time.","Skip the bathroom, so you finish at the original time.","Say nothing to anyone and just start the job one hour late."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":327},{"q":"The label says one cap of cleaner in a bucket of water. What do you do?","opts":["Pour it straight on the floor, because it works faster that way.","Use three caps for extra strength on the very dirty areas.","Use half a cap to save product for the next customer.","Use exactly one cap, because more can damage surfaces and be unsafe."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":328},{"q":"You think your salary is lower than promised. What do you do?","opts":["Complain loudly to the other cleaners at the accommodation.","Work slowly until the company fixes the salary.","Ask the customer for some extra money.","Show the details to HR politely and ask them to check."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":329},{"q":"The customer says, \"Skip the bathroom and I will give you cash.\" What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse, and clean the bathroom as booked.","Accept the cash and clean the bathroom very quickly.","Accept the cash and skip the bathroom completely.","Accept the cash and say nothing to anyone."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":330},{"q":"How do you clean the rubber seal of a fridge?","opts":["Wipe with mild soapy water and a soft cloth, then dry.","Ignore it, because the seal is not visible.","Use bleach and leave it on the seal for hours, so you finish sooner.","Scrub it hard with a hard brush until it is white."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":331},{"q":"The van has no air conditioning and you feel very hot. What do you do?","opts":["Skip the next job so you can rest.","Say nothing and keep working in the heat.","Drink water, tell the supervisor, and report the problem.","Complain to the customer about the van, because it is easier."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":332},{"q":"The customer leaves cash on the table and goes out. What do you do?","opts":["Leave it there and say nothing to the supervisor at all.","Do not touch it, clean around it, and tell the supervisor if you are worried.","Count it so that she knows it was all there when she returns.","Put it in a drawer so that it stays safe while she is out."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":333},{"q":"How do you clean a dirty iron plate?","opts":["Make sure it is cool and unplugged, then wipe gently as the label says.","Wash it under the tap while it is plugged in.","Use steel wool to scratch the dirt away.","Scrub it while it is still hot, so the dirt comes off."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":334},{"q":"A customer complains about a mistake that your partner made, and blames you. What do you do?","opts":["Argue loudly until the customer stops talking, because it is quicker.","Say sorry and accept all the blame yourself.","Blame your partner in front of the customer.","Stay calm, explain politely, and tell the supervisor what happened."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":335},{"q":"A colleague asks you to say they were with you when they were late. What do you do?","opts":["Lie for them, to help a friend.","Say you do not know, even if you do.","Cover for them this time, and warn them after, to save time.","Refuse to lie, and tell the supervisor the truth if asked."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":336},{"q":"How do you mop around furniture?","opts":["Push heavy furniture alone, so that you can mop under it.","Skip those areas, because they are hard to reach with the mop.","Move light items if allowed, mop around legs carefully, and put items back.","Leave the items in new places when you finish, to save time."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":337},{"q":"The customer asks you to wash her dishes, which are not in the booking. What do you do?","opts":["Wash them quickly, because it is only a few dishes.","Explain it is not in the booking, and suggest she books it through the company.","Refuse rudely and say it is not your job.","Wash a few dishes and leave the rest."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":338},{"q":"A colleague posts a photo of a customer's home in the cleaners' group chat. What do you do?","opts":["Comment on the customer's home in the chat.","Laugh about it and ignore the photo.","Share it with others in the group, because it is easier.","Ask them to delete it, and report it to the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":339},{"q":"A child's room has toys, a dusty shelf and a rug. Which order is best?","opts":["Dust the shelf, then vacuum, then tidy the toys.","Tidy the toys, dust the shelf, then vacuum the rug last.","Throw away the broken toys, then dust.","Vacuum the rug first, then tidy the toys."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":340},{"q":"The customer says you folded the towels the wrong way and asks you to redo them. What do you do?","opts":["Redo them, but complain about it while you work.","Tell her that the way you folded them is correct.","Ask how she likes them, and redo them politely.","Leave them as they are, because they look fine."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":341},{"q":"The customer says her old cleaner used strong acid on marble and asks you to do the same. What do you do?","opts":["Politely decline and use a stone-safe method.","Use it, but dilute it with some water first.","Use it, because the customer approves and is the owner.","Use it on a small area first, then continue."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":342},{"q":"How do you clean behind a toilet?","opts":["Spray a toilet cloth with disinfectant, wipe behind and the base, and dry.","Skip it, because it is hard to reach.","Use the mop only, and leave the rest.","Use the same cloth you used for the sink."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":343},{"q":"The customer says the job is not clean enough and wants a refund. What do you do?","opts":["Leave quickly, to avoid a long argument.","Argue that the job is clean, and show her the room.","Offer her a refund yourself, to end the discussion.","Stay calm, listen, offer to fix visible problems, and tell the supervisor."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":344},{"q":"Why do you wipe taps dry after cleaning?","opts":["Drying taps is not needed, because water is clean.","Wet taps look cleaner, so you leave them wet.","Dry wiping prevents water spots and limescale marks.","It uses less cloth if you leave the water."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":345},{"q":"The customer asks you to open her mail and read it to her. What do you do?","opts":["Open it and take a photo, so she can read later.","Open it and tell her only what you see on top, because it is less work.","Open it and read it to her, because she asked.","Politely decline, because personal papers are private."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":346},{"q":"Cleaners at the next job say they will leave early and tell the supervisor it was done. What do you do?","opts":["Join them, because they all agree and it is easy.","Stay but say nothing to the supervisor about it.","Join them, but come back later to finish.","Do not join, and finish your booked time."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":347},{"q":"How do you care for mop heads?","opts":["Use them for toilets and kitchens, to save money.","Throw them away after only one job.","Rinse them after use, wash by label, and let them dry fully.","Keep them wet in the bag between jobs, because it is quicker."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":348},{"q":"The customer asks you what you think of her husband. What do you do?","opts":["Ask her questions about him, to keep the talk going.","Politely say you cannot give opinions, and return to your work.","Share what you think, because she asked you directly.","Share a small joke about him, to be friendly."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":349},{"q":"A colleague asks you to pour your chemicals into their empty water bottle. What do you do?","opts":["Pour it and write the name on the water bottle, so you finish sooner.","Pour it for them, because they asked politely.","Refuse, because chemicals must stay in labelled bottles.","Pour a little, because they only need a small amount."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":350},{"q":"How do you clean a plastic garden chair?","opts":["Wipe with mild soapy water and a soft cloth, then dry.","Leave it wet, because the sun will dry it.","Scrub it with bleach until the chair is white.","Use a metal brush to remove all the dirt."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":351},{"q":"The customer gave the wrong address and the van drops you at another building. What do you do?","opts":["Ask a stranger to guide you to the right building.","Skip the job, because the driver made the mistake.","Walk to the customer's home yourself, without telling anyone.","Call the supervisor and wait for new instructions."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":352},{"q":"A colleague wants to leave a mess behind because the next job is easy. What do you do?","opts":["Say nothing and go back to the van.","Leave the mess too, because the next job is easy.","Clean it alone silently, and do not tell anyone, because it is less work.","Ask them to finish it properly, and tell the supervisor if they refuse."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":353},{"q":"How do you clean the outside of a cooker hood?","opts":["Use water only, because the hood is only a little dirty.","Wipe with degreaser on a cloth, then dry along the grain.","Use steel wool to remove the grease quickly, to save time.","Spray bleach all over it to remove the grease."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":354},{"q":"The trainer jokes about your mistake in front of others. What do you do?","opts":["Stay calm, fix the mistake, and speak to the trainer privately if it hurts.","Shout back, so the trainer stops joking about you.","Laugh with them, to hide that it hurts you.","Leave the group and go to your room."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":355},{"q":"A customer says, \"Write one hour less so I pay less.\" What do you do?","opts":["Politely refuse, and record the real time.","Say nothing and let her decide what to write.","Write half an hour less, as a compromise.","Write one hour less, because it is a small thing."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":356},{"q":"How do you clean a microwave plate?","opts":["Use bleach on the plate and put it back, because it is easier.","Remove it, wash with warm soapy water, rinse, and dry.","Wipe it with a dry cloth, and leave it as it is.","Leave it inside and clean only the walls."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":357},{"q":"A new cleaner asks you for help during the job and you are busy. What do you do?","opts":["Tell them to wait until the end of the day.","Do their work for them, so they do not worry.","Help briefly if possible, and tell the supervisor if more support is needed.","Ignore them, because you are busy with your own job."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":358},{"q":"A colleague sells their own cleaning products to customers. What do you do?","opts":["Ignore it, because it is not your problem.","Tell them it is not allowed, and report it to the supervisor.","Ask for a share of the money they earn, because it is less work.","Buy some, because they are cheaper than the company products."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":359},{"q":"A villa has a marble hall, carpeted bedrooms and a tiled kitchen. Which floor order is best?","opts":["Mop the kitchen first, then sweep the hall.","Use the same wet mop on every floor to save time.","Vacuum carpets and sweep first, then mop the kitchen and the marble hall, finishing at the exit.","Mop the marble hall first, then vacuum the carpets."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":360},{"q":"The customer comes home 40 minutes early while you are cleaning the bathroom, and she frowns at the mess. What do you do?","opts":["Stop and apologise for the mess several times.","Greet her politely, explain you are in the middle of cleaning, and keep working neatly.","Ask her to wait outside until you finish.","Hurry out of the bathroom and leave it half done."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":361},{"q":"The customer asks you to use her strong stain remover on her white marble sink. The label warns about stone. What do you do?","opts":["Politely decline, explain the label warning, and use a stone-safe method.","Dilute it with water and try a small area.","Use it quickly and rinse right away.","Use it, because she accepts any damage."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":362},{"q":"The bathroom extractor fan cover is dusty. What is the safe method?","opts":["Poke the dust with a metal spoon.","Wipe it while the fan is on.","Switch it off at the wall, remove the cover if it clips off, and wipe it clean.","Spray water into the fan while it is running."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":363},{"q":"Other cleaners say you work too hard and should slow down so the team looks fair. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer that the other cleaners are lazy and slow.","Keep to your normal quality and time plan, and politely ignore the pressure.","Work hard only when the supervisor is near you and watching.","Slow down to avoid any conflict with the other cleaners in the team."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":364},{"q":"How do you clean a granite kitchen sink?","opts":["Use mild soap and warm water with a soft cloth, then rinse and dry.","Soak it in acid cleaner overnight.","Wipe it with a dry cloth only.","Scrub with a wire brush and bleach."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":365},{"q":"You notice an old crack in the customer's bathroom sink before you start. What is the best thing to do?","opts":["Say nothing, because the crack was already there before you came.","Tell the supervisor and customer before you start, so you are not blamed later.","Fix it with some glue before you start, so it looks better.","Cover it with a towel, so that nobody sees it at all."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":366},{"q":"The customer does not answer your questions about which room to start with, and time is passing. What do you do?","opts":["Do only the easy rooms, and leave the hard ones.","Start with the main areas in the standard order, and tell her your plan.","Wait outside until she answers all your questions, because it is quicker.","Stop and call the supervisor every few minutes."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":367},{"q":"There are rust marks on a white tile floor. What do you do first?","opts":["Pour bleach on the marks and leave it overnight.","Scrub with steel wool until the rust marks go.","Cover the marks with a rug so nobody sees them.","Use a suitable rust remover for tiles by the label, test a hidden spot, and rinse well."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":368},{"q":"A friend wants to stay overnight in your accommodation room, but guests are not allowed. What do you do?","opts":["Politely say no, and ask the accommodation supervisor if you need a solution.","Hide them from the supervisor, so that nobody knows they stayed.","Let them stay for just one night, then ask them to stop.","Let them stay quietly, because it is only for one night."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":369},{"q":"The customer says, \"Please do not follow the steps you learned. Just do it my way fast.\" Her way is unsafe. What do you do?","opts":["Follow her way, to keep her happy and avoid trouble.","Follow her way only while she is watching you.","Politely explain you must follow the safe steps, and call the supervisor if she insists.","Mix both ways, so everyone is a little happy."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":370},{"q":"How do you clean a bin lid with sticky dirt?","opts":["Scrub it with a rough pad until it shines, to finish sooner.","Wipe with warm soapy water and a cloth, then rinse and dry.","Spray perfume on the lid to hide the smell.","Leave it to dry in the sun and move on."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":371},{"q":"You hear that another cleaner got a cash tip and hid it. A friend suggests you do the same next time. What do you do?","opts":["Refuse all tips and never mention them to anyone, to save time.","Take the tips and give half to the company.","Hide tips too, because other cleaners do the same.","Do not hide tips, and ask the supervisor what the tip rule is."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":372},{"q":"A customer asks you not to mention that her son broke a window while you were there. What do you do?","opts":["Agree, because it is not your fault that the window broke.","Fix the window quietly, so that nobody knows about it.","Report it honestly if the company asks, and politely say you cannot hide it.","Say nothing and leave when the job is finished, as usual."],"correct":2,"cat":"Tricky","id":373},{"q":"What do you do with a squeegee on a window?","opts":["Press hard and scrub, to remove the stains faster.","Pull the squeegee in circles over the glass, so you finish sooner.","Use the same wet blade without wiping it each time.","Wipe the blade clean after each pull and pull in straight lines."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":374},{"q":"The trainer changes the training time to a later hour and you have a personal appointment. What do you do?","opts":["Come late without telling the trainer or the supervisor, because it is less work.","Say you are sick, so you can go to your appointment.","Skip the training, because your appointment is more important.","Tell the trainer politely and ask if you can adjust, or follow the schedule."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":375},{"q":"A customer asks you to take photos of the bathroom before and after on your phone to send to her friend. What do you do?","opts":["Politely decline, and say photos must follow company rules.","Take them, and delete them from your phone later.","Take them and send them to her friend, because it is easier.","Take them, but avoid showing the sink and the toilet."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":376},{"q":"There are cobwebs in a high ceiling corner. What do you do?","opts":["Throw a cloth at it, to pull the cobweb down.","Stand on a table to reach the corner easily, because it is quicker.","Leave it, because nobody will see it up there.","Use an extendable duster from the floor or a stable step stool."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":377},{"q":"The driver stops at a shop for 30 minutes and you will be late for the job. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer about the delay only later, to save time.","Get out and walk to the job on your own.","Tell the driver about the time, and inform the supervisor.","Wait quietly in the van until the driver is ready."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":378},{"q":"A colleague offers you money if you do their job and sign their report. What do you do?","opts":["Refuse, and report it to the supervisor.","Accept, but sign only your own report.","Accept the money, because it is a private deal.","Ask for more money before you agree to do it."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":379},{"q":"In a baby's room with a cot, a changing table and a floor, which order is best?","opts":["Vacuum first, then dust the cot.","Dust surfaces first, wipe the table with a safe cleaner, then vacuum the floor last.","Wipe the table, then dust the shelves.","Use strong disinfectant on the cot first."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":380},{"q":"The customer asks you to stop in the middle of the job because she must leave. What do you do?","opts":["Stay polite, note what was finished, and call the supervisor.","Leave quickly without saying anything to her.","Finish the job anyway and ignore what she says.","Ask her to pay you now for the part done, so you finish sooner."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":381},{"q":"The customer asks you to spray strong disinfectant on a cutting board you will not rinse. What do you do?","opts":["Spray just a little, so it is not too strong.","Spray it and leave it to dry without rinsing, because it is less work.","Spray it, because the customer asked you to do it.","Politely explain it must be rinsed well with clean water before use."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":382},{"q":"How do you clean a kitchen tap with limescale?","opts":["Wipe it with a wet cloth and leave it.","Use a knife to scrape the limescale off.","Use strong toilet acid, because it works fastest.","Use a mild descaler by the label, rinse, and polish with a soft cloth."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":383},{"q":"The customer stands behind you and corrects every move. What do you do?","opts":["Tell her to stop and leave you alone.","Do everything she says, in her order, because it is easier.","Stay calm, listen to her, and continue to work as trained.","Stop working until she is quiet."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":384},{"q":"What do you check before using a ladder?","opts":["Stand on the top step to reach more.","Use it on a rug, because it is soft.","Lean it on a glass door so it stays still.","Check it is stable and on a flat floor, and never use it alone if it is too tall."],"correct":3,"cat":"Skills","id":385},{"q":"A colleague takes extra time resting and asks you to cover. What do you do?","opts":["Tell the customer that your colleague is resting.","Politely refuse, and tell the supervisor if it continues.","Cover for them, because they are tired today.","Rest too, so the team stays fair."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":386},{"q":"The van says it cannot come because of rain. What do you do?","opts":["Walk home in the rain, to save time.","Skip your next job, since the rain is too bad.","Wait safely and follow the supervisor's instructions.","Take a random lift from a stranger on the road."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":387},{"q":"How do you freshen a customer's mattress?","opts":["Beat it hard with a stick to remove dust.","Pour water on it to refresh it quickly, so you finish sooner.","Vacuum it, then follow the company method for spot cleaning.","Spray strong chemicals on it, to kill the smell."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":388},{"q":"Your new schedule starts earlier and you feel tired. What do you do?","opts":["Say you are sick, so you can sleep more.","Stay home on the day the schedule begins, to finish sooner.","Arrive late every day, because you are tired.","Follow it, and talk to the supervisor about your concerns."],"correct":3,"cat":"Situational","id":389},{"q":"A customer asks for your personal number to book you for private jobs. What do you do?","opts":["Give her a friend's number, so you stay safe.","Politely decline, and say bookings go through the company.","Give her your number, because it is easy and helpful.","Say you will think about it, and call her later, to save time."],"correct":1,"cat":"Tricky","id":390},{"q":"How do you remove mould from wall tiles?","opts":["Mix different cleaners together to make it stronger.","Wear a mask and gloves, ventilate, and use a suitable cleaner by the label.","Dry scrub the mould with a brush, without a mask.","Paint over the mould, so nobody sees it."],"correct":1,"cat":"Skills","id":391},{"q":"The customer must leave and asks you to finish in 10 minutes. What do you do?","opts":["Say you cannot do anything in that time, because it is less work.","Rush everything, so each room is touched a little.","Tell her what you can finish well, and finish the visible areas.","Leave, because the time is too short."],"correct":2,"cat":"Situational","id":392},{"q":"A colleague wants to skip the machine and says nobody will know. What do you do?","opts":["Use the machine as trained, and report if they keep skipping it.","Use the machine only once, then stop.","Say nothing and finish the job as they do, because it is quicker.","Skip the machine too, since nobody will know."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":393},{"q":"How do you dust books on a shelf?","opts":["Use a soft brush or dry microfiber, and wipe the shelf last.","Shake the books in the room to remove dust, to finish sooner.","Spray cleaner directly on the books.","Use a wet cloth on the books to remove dust."],"correct":0,"cat":"Skills","id":394},{"q":"You call the supervisor about a problem and there is no answer. What do you do?","opts":["Leave the job and go home.","Try again, send a clear message, and keep safe while waiting.","Ignore the problem and wait for it to go away.","Ask the customer to decide what you should do."],"correct":1,"cat":"Situational","id":395},{"q":"A customer asks you to say you are her friend if her neighbour asks. What do you do?","opts":["Say you are from the cleaning company, and do not pretend.","Say you are her friend, as she asked.","Say you are her relative from another country.","Say nothing and walk away from the neighbour, to save time."],"correct":0,"cat":"Tricky","id":396},{"q":"How do you clean a ceramic hob?","opts":["Use bleach on the hob to make it white.","Use steel wool to scrub the hob clean, because it is less work.","Let it cool, then use a suitable hob cleaner and a soft cloth.","Clean the hob while it is still hot."],"correct":2,"cat":"Skills","id":397},{"q":"A group chat spreads gossip about the supervisor. What do you do?","opts":["Do not join, and raise concerns with the supervisor or HR.","Join the gossip, to avoid feeling left out.","Reply angrily in the group, to defend the supervisor.","Leave the group and say nothing to anyone."],"correct":0,"cat":"Situational","id":398},{"q":"A colleague asks you to tell them your salary and bonus. What do you do?","opts":["Lie about your pay, so they do not ask more.","Share half of the details, to be fair.","Share the details, because they are your friend.","Politely say you do not share pay details."],"correct":3,"cat":"Tricky","id":399}];
